</table>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In addition, we study the following smooth nonconvex-strongly-concave minimax optimization problem</p>
<table id="S1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\max_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}f(x,y)\coloneqq{\mathbb{E}}[F(x,y;\xi)]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\max_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}f(x,y)\coloneqq{\mathbb{E}}[F(x,y;\xi)],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\colon{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}\times{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}\to{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\colon{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}\times{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}\to{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonconvex in <math id="S1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and strongly-concave in <math id="S1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Most of the existing works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite> on stochastic minimax optimization under the heavy-tailed noise assume the objective is convex-concave.
For the more general setting, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gorbunov et al. [23]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sadiev et al. [56]</a></cite> consider the problem under the star-cocoercive condition, while their results does not contain the popular nonconvex-strongly-concave case.
To address this gap, we propose an efficient stochastic first-order method called nested-loop normalized stochastic gradient descent ascent (N<sup id="S1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA) for solving the problem (<a href="#S1.E6" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) under the <math id="S1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-BCM gradient noise condition.
We show that N<sup id="S1.p6.2.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA achieves an <math id="S1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point of the function <math id="S1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(x)\coloneqq\max_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x)\coloneqq\max_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> within a stochastic first-order oracle (SFO) complexity of <math id="S1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}\big(\kappa^{\frac{2p-1}{p-1}}\sigma_{f}^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\epsilon^{-\frac{3p-2}{p-1}}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}\big(\kappa^{\frac{2p-1}{p-1}}\sigma_{f}^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\epsilon^{-\frac{3p-2}{p-1}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> both in expectation and with high probability.
This result yields nearly optimal dependence on <math id="S1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, aligning with the known lower bound of <math id="S1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\sigma_{f}^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\epsilon^{-\frac{3p-2}{p-1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\sigma_{f}^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\epsilon^{-\frac{3p-2}{p-1}})</annotation></semantics></math> up to a logarithmic factor for stochastic first-order algorithms in general nonconvex optimization under <math id="S1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-BCM noise <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite>.
We compare the proposed methods with existing work for solving the minimax optimization problem in Table <a href="#S1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Paper Organization</h5>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S2" title="2 Related Work ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we provide a literature review of stochastic bilevel optimization and the minimization and minimax optimization problems.
In Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we introduce some preliminaries on stationarity concepts relevant to bilevel optimization and minimax optimization problems.
In Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Stochastic Bilevel Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we propose our N<sup id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA algorithm for solving the nonconvex-strongly-convex bilevel optimization problem, and establish both its in-expectation and high-probability convergence guarantee.
In Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Stochastic Minimax Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we propose the N<sup id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA method to solve the nonconvex-strongly-concave minimax optimization problem that obtains nearly optimal SFO complexity.
In Section <a href="#S6" title="6 Experiments ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we conduct numerical experiments to validate the effectiveness of our proposed approaches.
Finally, we conclude our work and outline several potential directions for future research in Section <a href="#S7" title="7 Conclusion and Future Work ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Related Work</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a review of related work on stochastic methods for bilevel optimization, along with stochastic minimization and minimax optimization problems in the presence of heavy-tailed noise.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Stochastic methods for Bilevel and Minimax Optimization </h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To address the stochastic bilevel optimization problem, earlier HVP-based approaches <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> construct the stochastic hyper-gradient estimator explicitly according to the update (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
These methods employ iterative algorithms to solve the associated linear system, thereby avoiding the explicit computation of the costly Hessian inverse.
In particular, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ghadimi and Wang [19]</a></cite> proposed the bilevel stochastic approximation (BSA) method based on single-sample gradient and Hessian estimates. Building on this, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hong et al. [28]</a></cite> developed a two-timescale stochastic approximation (TTSA) algorithm that achieves a better trade-off between the complexities of the inner and outer optimization loops.
Later, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ji et al. [30]</a></cite> designed a more sample-efficient hyper-gradient estimator using the Neumann series.
Very recently, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hao et al. [27]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gong et al. [20]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gong et al. [21]</a></cite> established high-probability convergence guarantees of HVP-based methods for stochastic bilevel optimization with unbounded smoothness under the light-tailed noise assumption.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The gradient-based stochastic methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> leverage inexpensive gradient oracles while avoiding reliance on costly HVP oracle evaluations, thereby enhancing their scalability to large-scale bilevel optimization problems.
Observing that <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> in equation (<a href="#S1.E5" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) involves only first-order information, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. [42]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shen and Chen [57]</a></cite> proposed deterministic algorithms that converge to a stationary point of <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, but without establishing any convergence guarantees for <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Building on this, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al. [35]</a></cite> established the relationship between <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and introduced the Fully First-order Stochastic Approximation (F<sup id="S2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SA) method to obtain an approximate stationary point of <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
More recently, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. [4]</a></cite> incorporated a two-timescale update to enhance F<sup id="S2.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SA, achieving a stochastic first-order (SFO) complexity of <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}(\kappa^{11}\sigma^{2}\epsilon^{-6})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>11</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}(\kappa^{11}\sigma^{2}\epsilon^{-6})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For stochastic minimax optimization, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al. [32]</a></cite> proposed the stochastic gradient descent with max-oracle (SGDmax) method, which adopts a nested-loop framework: the inner loop approximately solves the maximization subproblem <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the obtained solution is then utilized in the outer loop to perform an approximate stochastic gradient descent update on <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.
 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al. [40]</a></cite> demonstrated that the problem (<a href="#S1.E6" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) can be solved by directly extending stochastic gradient descent (SGD) to the stochastic gradient descent ascent (SGDA) method, which performs gradient descent on <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and gradient ascent on <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.
In contrast to SGDmax, which relies on an inner maximization loop, SGDA updates both variables simultaneously.
They further established that SGDA requires <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}(\kappa^{3}\sigma_{f}^{2}\epsilon^{-4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}(\kappa^{3}\sigma_{f}^{2}\epsilon^{-4})</annotation></semantics></math> stochastic gradient evaluations to obtain an <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point of <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> in expectation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Minimization and Minimax Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Classical in expectation and high probability convergence guarantees for convex problems are derived under the assumption of light-tailed noise distribution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>, <a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nazin et al. [47]</a></cite> established the first high-probability complexity bounds for convex optimization under the assumption of bounded gradient variance.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gorbunov et al. [22]</a></cite> introduced the technique of accelerated gradient clipping, leading to improved complexity bounds for both convex and strongly convex settings.
Subsequent work by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gorbunov et al. [25]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sadiev et al. [56]</a></cite> extended these approaches to the problem with Hölder-continuous gradients under weaker heavy-tailed noise assumptions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Compared with the convex problem, the study of nonconvex problems under heavy-tailed noise is relatively scarce.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. [63]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sadiev et al. [56]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nguyen et al. [50]</a></cite> studied in-expectation and high probability convergence guarantee of Clip-SGD under <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-BCM noise assumption.
However, these studies employ an increasing clipping parameter, which results in suboptimal convergence guarantees.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cutkosky and Mehta [8]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu and Zhou [44]</a></cite> attained improved complexity bounds by leveraging a combination of gradient normalization and clipping under some restrictive assumptions.
Very recently, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hübler et al. [29]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu and Zhou [45]</a></cite> investigated the normalized stochastic gradient descent method, demonstrating that it attains an optimal complexity bound under the <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-BCM noise assumption without the gradient clipping technique.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the minimax optimization problem, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Juditsky et al. [33]</a></cite> established the first in-expectation and high probability complexity bound for solving monotone variation inequality (VI) assuming the noise is light-tailed.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gorbunov et al. [23]</a></cite> derived high probability complexity results of stochastic methods for solving monotone VI problems under the bounded gradient variance assumption.
Later, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sadiev et al. [56]</a></cite> extended their result to the <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-BCM noise distribution setting.
While both studies address the non-monotone star-cocoercive variational inequality problems, their results do not generalize to the nonconvex-strongly-concave setting.
Very recently, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Laguel et al. [37]</a></cite> provided high probability complexity results for the nonconvex-Polyak-Lojasiewicz problem under the light-tailed noise assumption.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Preliminaries</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present the assumptions used throughout the paper, and then we introduce the definitions of stationarities of the bilevel and minimax optimization problems.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by outlining the assumptions necessary for finding first-order stationary points of the hyper-objective <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmasm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_asm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmasm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmasm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmasm1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmasm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmasm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{g}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-gradient Lipschitz, </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{g}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-Hessian Lipschitz, and </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-strongly convex in </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-Lipschitz in </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{f}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-gradient Lipschitz, and two-times continuous differentiable;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is lower bounded, </span><em id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">i.e.</em><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\varphi(x)&gt;-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\varphi(x)&gt;-\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The above assumptions are standard and essential for non-asymptotic analyses of bilevel optimization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.
As established in Theorem 3.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. [3]</a></cite>, bilevel problems are generally intractable when <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is not strongly convex. Consequently, existing non-asymptotic analyses of bilevel optimization typically adopt the lower-level strong convexity assumption.
Under this assumption, the hyper-gradient <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed in terms of <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{x}f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{x}f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{y}f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{y}f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{xy}^{2}g(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{xy}^{2}g(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{yy}^{2}g(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{yy}^{2}g(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> as shown in Equation <a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
We define the condition number of the problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmdfn1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_dfn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmdfn1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmdfn1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmdfn1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmdfn1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmdfn1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we define the largest smoothness constant <math id="S3.Thmdfn1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell:=\max\{C_{f},L_{f},L_{g},\rho_{g}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell:=\max\{C_{f},L_{f},L_{g},\rho_{g}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the condition number of problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) as <math id="S3.Thmdfn1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa:=\ell/\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa:=\ell/\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">From the above assumptions, it follows that <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely defined and Lipschitz continuous, as formally stated below.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmprop1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmprop1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmprop1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">L</span></cite>emma 2.2)<span id="S3.Thmprop1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmprop1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmprop1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmprop1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ghadimi2018approximation]

Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>,
the hyper-gradient <math id="S3.Thmprop1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely defined by Equation <a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, and
the hyper-objective <math id="S3.Thmprop1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.Thmprop1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\varphi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>φ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\varphi}</annotation></semantics></math>-gradient Lipschitz, where <math id="S3.Thmprop1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\varphi}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>φ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\varphi}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Since the above proposition guarantees that the gradient of the hyper-objective <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined, we define the notion of <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-first-order stationary points as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmdfn2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_dfn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmdfn2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmdfn2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmdfn2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmdfn2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmdfn2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a differentiable function <math id="S3.Thmdfn2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x):{\mathbb{R}}^{d}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x):{\mathbb{R}}^{d}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we call <math id="S3.Thmdfn2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}</annotation></semantics></math> an <math id="S3.Thmdfn2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-first-order stationary point of <math id="S3.Thmdfn2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S3.Thmdfn2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\varphi(\hat{x})\|\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\varphi(\hat{x})\|\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We note that evaluating the hyper-gradient <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> requires computing both the Jacobian and the inverse of the Hessian, which can be prohibitively expensive in large-scale bilevel optimization.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al. [35]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. [4]</a></cite> observed that the gradient <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> can be evaluated using only first-order information, and further established its relationship with <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, as stated below.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmlem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmlem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmlem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. [4]</a></cite>)<span id="S3.Thmlem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmlem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmlem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmlem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, for <math id="S3.Thmlem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 2L_{f}/\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 2L_{f}/\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|y^{*}_{\lambda}(x)-y^{*}(x)\right\|\leq{C_{f}}/{(\lambda\mu)},~~~~|L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)-\phi(x)|\leq D_{0}/\lambda," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.487em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|y^{*}_{\lambda}(x)-y^{*}(x)\right\|\leq{C_{f}}/{(\lambda\mu)},~~~~|L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)-\phi(x)|\leq D_{0}/\lambda,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)-\nabla\phi(x)\right\|\leq D_{1}/\lambda,~~~\left\|\nabla y^{*}(x)-\nabla y_{\lambda}^{*}(x)\right\|\leq D_{2}/\lambda," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)-\nabla\phi(x)\right\|\leq D_{1}/\lambda,~~~\left\|\nabla y^{*}(x)-\nabla y_{\lambda}^{*}(x)\right\|\leq D_{2}/\lambda,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmlem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmlem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where we define</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{0}\coloneqq\left(C_{f}\!+\!\frac{C_{f}L_{g}}{2\mu}\right)\frac{C_{f}}{\mu}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{2}),~~~D_{1}\coloneqq\left(L_{f}\!+\!\frac{\rho_{g}L_{g}}{\mu}\!+\!\frac{C_{f}L_{g}\rho_{g}}{2\mu^{2}}\!+\!\frac{C_{f}\rho_{g}}{2\mu}\right)\frac{C_{f}}{\mu}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{3})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{0}\coloneqq\left(C_{f}\!+\!\frac{C_{f}L_{g}}{2\mu}\right)\frac{C_{f}}{\mu}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{2}),~~~D_{1}\coloneqq\left(L_{f}\!+\!\frac{\rho_{g}L_{g}}{\mu}\!+\!\frac{C_{f}L_{g}\rho_{g}}{2\mu^{2}}\!+\!\frac{C_{f}\rho_{g}}{2\mu}\right)\frac{C_{f}}{\mu}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{3}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{2}\coloneqq\left(\frac{1}{\mu}+\frac{2L_{g}}{\mu^{2}}\right)\left(L_{f}+\frac{C_{f}\rho_{g}}{\mu}\right)={\mathcal{O}}(\kappa^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{2}\coloneqq\left(\frac{1}{\mu}+\frac{2L_{g}}{\mu^{2}}\right)\left(L_{f}+\frac{C_{f}\rho_{g}}{\mu}\right)={\mathcal{O}}(\kappa^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Based on Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 3.1 ( [ ] ). ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, by setting <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\Theta(\epsilon^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\Theta(\epsilon^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, any <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point of <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to an <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point of <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Approximate Stationary Points of Minimax Optimization</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now state the assumptions required to establish first-order stationary points of the minimax optimization problem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmasm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_asm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmasm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmasm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmasm2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmasm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmasm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the objective function satisfies</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">a.</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-smooth and </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-strongly concave.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">b.</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is uniformly lower bounded, i.e., </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\max_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}f(x,y)&gt;-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\max_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}f(x,y)&gt;-\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The above assumptions are standard and essential for non-asymptotic analyses of the nonconvex-strongly-concave minimax optimization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>, <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>.
For the ease of notation, we define</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(\cdot)=\max_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}f(\cdot,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\cdot)=\max_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}f(\cdot,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We observe that the minimax optimization problem (<a href="#S1.E6" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) can be equivalently reformulated as the minimization of the objective function <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, when <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is nonconvex in <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and strongly concave in <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, the resulting function <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is guaranteed to be smooth.
To make this precise, we formally state the following technical lemma, which establishes the structural properties of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmprop2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmprop2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmprop2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al. [40, Lemma 4.3]</a></cite>)<span id="S3.Thmprop2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmprop2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmprop2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmprop2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm2" title="Assumption 3.2. ‣ 3.2 Approximate Stationary Points of Minimax Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, <math id="S3.Thmprop2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.Thmprop2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ell+\kappa\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ell+\kappa\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth with <math id="S3.Thmprop2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\Phi(\cdot)=\nabla_{x}f(\cdot,y^{*}(\cdot))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\Phi(\cdot)=\nabla_{x}f(\cdot,y^{*}(\cdot))</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.Thmprop2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\coloneqq\ell/\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\coloneqq\ell/\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is the condition number and <math id="S3.Thmprop2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}(\cdot)=\argmax_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}f(\cdot,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}(\cdot)=\argmax_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}f(\cdot,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In addition, <math id="S3.Thmprop2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.Thmprop2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since the function <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is nonconvex, finding its global minimum is generally NP-hard.
Consequently, our objective is to seek its approximate stationary points instead.
Formally, we define the notion of an <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-first-order stationary point as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmdfn3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_dfn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmdfn3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmdfn3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmdfn3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmdfn3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmdfn3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We call a point <math id="S3.Thmdfn3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}</annotation></semantics></math> an <math id="S3.Thmdfn3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point of a differentiable function <math id="S3.Thmdfn3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> if it satisfies <math id="S3.Thmdfn3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\nabla\Phi(\hat{x})\right\|\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\nabla\Phi(\hat{x})\right\|\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Stochastic Gradient Assumption</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before concluding this section, we formally introduce the <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-th bounded central moment (<math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-BCM) assumption on the stochastic gradient oracle, which generalizes the conventional bounded variance assumption.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmasm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_asm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmasm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmasm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmasm3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmasm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmasm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We access the gradients of the bilevel problem in equation (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) via the unbiased gradient oracle <math id="S3.Thmasm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla F(x,y;\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla F(x,y;\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmasm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla G(x,y;\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla G(x,y;\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\nabla F(x,y;\xi)]=\nabla f(x,y),~~~{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla F(x,y;\xi)-\nabla f(x,y)\right\|^{p}]\leq\sigma_{f}^{p}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\nabla F(x,y;\xi)]=\nabla f(x,y),~~~{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla F(x,y;\xi)-\nabla f(x,y)\right\|^{p}]\leq\sigma_{f}^{p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\nabla G(x,y;\zeta)]=\nabla g(x,y),~~~{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla G(x,y;\zeta)-\nabla g(x,y)\right\|^{p}]\leq\sigma_{g}^{p}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\nabla G(x,y;\zeta)]=\nabla g(x,y),~~~{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla G(x,y;\zeta)-\nabla g(x,y)\right\|^{p}]\leq\sigma_{g}^{p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmasm3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmasm3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S3.Thmasm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in(1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(1,2]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmasm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{f},\sigma_{g}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{f},\sigma_{g}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the minimax optimization problem (<a href="#S1.E6" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), we access an unbiased gradient oracle <math id="S3.Thmasm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla F(x,y;\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla F(x,y;\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies condition (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Stochastic Gradient Assumption ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce the variable <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=\max\{\sigma_{f},\sigma_{g}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\max\{\sigma_{f},\sigma_{g}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for the bilevel optimization problem, while for the minimax optimization problem, we simply set <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=\sigma_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\sigma_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> to simplify the notation.
We remark that Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Stochastic Gradient Assumption ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> with <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=2</annotation></semantics></math> aligns with the classical bounded variance condition.
For the general case of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in(1,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(1,2)</annotation></semantics></math>, the variance of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla F(x,y;\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla F(x,y;\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla G(x,y;\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla G(x,y;\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math> are possibly unbounded.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Stochastic Bilevel Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we introduce a stochastic first-order algorithm for solving the nonconvex–strongly-convex bilevel optimization problem under heavy-tailed noise, and we provide convergence guarantees both in expectation and with high probability.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>The Algorithm</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Nested-loop Normalized Stochastic Bilevel Approximation (N<sup id="alg1.5" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}},\hat{y}_{0,0}=\hat{z}_{0,0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}},\hat{y}_{0,0}=\hat{z}_{0,0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, stepsize <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{x},\eta_{y,t},\eta_{z,t}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{x},\eta_{y,t},\eta_{z,t}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, sequences of clipping parameters <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tau_{t,k}\}_{k=0}^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tau_{t,k}\}_{k=0}^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tau_{t,k}^{\prime}\}_{k=0}^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tau_{t,k}^{\prime}\}_{k=0}^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T,K,M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T,K,M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,\dots,T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,\dots,T-1</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,\dots,K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,\dots,K-1</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
               draw data sample <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{z,t,k}=\lambda\nabla_{y}G(x_{t},\hat{z}_{t,k};\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{z,t,k}=\lambda\nabla_{y}G(x_{t},\hat{z}_{t,k};\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}_{t,k+1}=\hat{z}_{t,k}-\eta_{z,t}{\rm clip}(g_{z,t,k},\tau_{t,k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>clip</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}_{t,k+1}=\hat{z}_{t,k}-\eta_{z,t}{\rm clip}(g_{z,t,k},\tau_{t,k})</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{y,t,k}=\nabla_{y}F(x_{t},\hat{y}_{t,k};\xi^{\prime})+\lambda\nabla_{y}G(x_{t},\hat{y}_{t,k};\zeta^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{y,t,k}=\nabla_{y}F(x_{t},\hat{y}_{t,k};\xi^{\prime})+\lambda\nabla_{y}G(x_{t},\hat{y}_{t,k};\zeta^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{t,k+1}=\hat{y}_{t,k}-\eta_{y,t}{\rm clip}(g_{y,t,k},\tau_{t,k}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>clip</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{t,k+1}=\hat{y}_{t,k}-\eta_{y,t}{\rm clip}(g_{y,t,k},\tau_{t,k}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end for</span> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}=\hat{y}_{t,K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}=\hat{y}_{t,K}</annotation></semantics></math>,    <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{t+1,0}=\hat{y}_{t,K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{t+1,0}=\hat{y}_{t,K}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}=\hat{z}_{t,K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}=\hat{z}_{t,K}</annotation></semantics></math>,    <math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}_{t+1,0}=\hat{z}_{t,K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}_{t+1,0}=\hat{z}_{t,K}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
              draw a collection of <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> data samples <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\xi_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\xi_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\zeta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\zeta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{g_{x,t}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}}\left[\nabla_{x}F(x_{t},y_{t};\xi_{i})+\lambda(\nabla_{x}G(x_{t},y_{t};\zeta_{i})-\nabla_{x}G(x_{t},z_{t};\zeta_{i}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{g_{x,t}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}}\left[\nabla_{x}F(x_{t},y_{t};\xi_{i})+\lambda(\nabla_{x}G(x_{t},y_{t};\zeta_{i})-\nabla_{x}G(x_{t},z_{t};\zeta_{i}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}=x_{t}-\eta_{x}\cdot\dfrac{g_{x,t}}{\left\|g_{x,t}\right\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}=x_{t}-\eta_{x}\cdot\dfrac{g_{x,t}}{\left\|g_{x,t}\right\|}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end for</span> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
             draw <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return:</span> <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce our nested-loop normalized stochastic bilevel approximation (N<sup id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA) in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.1 The Algorithm ‣ 4 Stochastic Bilevel Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
The algorithm incorporates an auxiliary variable <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and applies variants of stochastic gradient descent (SGD) updates simultaneously to <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> in order to solve the following optimization problem:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}},y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}\left\{f(x,y)+\lambda\left(g(x,y)-\min_{z\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}g(x,z)\right)\right\}\overset{(\ref{eq:L-lambda})}{=}\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S1.E4" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></mtext><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}},y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}\left\{f(x,y)+\lambda\left(g(x,y)-\min_{z\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}g(x,z)\right)\right\}\overset{(\ref{eq:L-lambda})}{=}\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, our algorithm employs a nested-loop structure: the outer loop functions as an inexact stochastic gradient descent on the nonconvex function <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, while the inner loop computes approximate solutions of <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda g(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda g(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> separately.
However, as noted in Remark 1 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. [63]</a></cite>, a naive application of SGD to this problem may fail to converge in the presence of heavy-tailed noise.
To address this issue, we apply gradient clipping to the stochastic gradients of equation (<a href="#S4.E10" title="In 4.1 The Algorithm ‣ 4 Stochastic Bilevel Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) evaluated at <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> within the inner loop. Specifically, the clipping operator with parameter <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\rm clip}(x,\tau)=\begin{cases}\min\left\{1,{\tau}/{\left\|x\right\|}\right\}x,&amp;x\neq 0,\\
0,&amp;x=0,\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\rm clip}(x,\tau)=\begin{cases}\min\left\{1,{\tau}/{\left\|x\right\|}\right\}x,&amp;x\neq 0,\\
0,&amp;x=0,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which prevents excessively large stochastic gradients arising from heavy-tailed noise.
For the outer loop, however, applying gradient clipping alone to the stochastic gradient at <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> often leads to suboptimal convergence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>.
To address this, we instead perform a single step of normalized stochastic gradient descent on <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In contrast to classical nonconvex optimization, bilevel optimization does not provide access to an unbiased gradient estimator of the outer-level function, which motivates us to normalize the inexact stochastic gradient estimator and perform a single gradient descent step with respect to <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Convergence Analysis</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we present the complexity results of N<sup id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA for solving the nonconvex-strongly-convex bilevel optimization problem.
As discussed in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, our objective is to identify an <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, which corresponds to an <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> with an appropriate choice of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmasm3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Stochastic Gradient Assumption ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, running Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.1 The Algorithm ‣ 4 Stochastic Bilevel Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (N<sup id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA) with</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta_{x}=\frac{\epsilon}{\ell\kappa^{3}},~~~\eta_{y,t}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{400(L_{f}+\lambda L_{g})},\frac{2\ln(B_{y,t})}{\lambda\mu K}\right\},~~~\eta_{z,t}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{400\lambda L_{g}},\frac{\ln(B_{z,t})}{\lambda\mu K}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta_{x}=\frac{\epsilon}{\ell\kappa^{3}},~~~\eta_{y,t}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{400(L_{f}+\lambda L_{g})},\frac{2\ln(B_{y,t})}{\lambda\mu K}\right\},~~~\eta_{z,t}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{400\lambda L_{g}},\frac{\ln(B_{z,t})}{\lambda\mu K}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta\ell\kappa^{3}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right),~~~M={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{3p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right),~~~K=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{4p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta\ell\kappa^{3}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right),~~~M={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{3p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right),~~~K=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{4p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau_{t,k}=\frac{\exp(-\eta_{z,t}\lambda\mu(1/2+k/4))R_{z}}{120\eta_{z,t}},~~~\tau_{t,k}^{\prime}=\frac{\exp(-\eta_{y,t}\lambda\mu(1+k/2))R_{y}}{120\eta_{y,t}},~~~\lambda=\max\left\{\frac{\kappa}{R_{0}},\frac{\ell\kappa^{2}}{\Delta},\frac{\ell\kappa^{3}}{\epsilon}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>120</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>120</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau_{t,k}=\frac{\exp(-\eta_{z,t}\lambda\mu(1/2+k/4))R_{z}}{120\eta_{z,t}},~~~\tau_{t,k}^{\prime}=\frac{\exp(-\eta_{y,t}\lambda\mu(1+k/2))R_{y}}{120\eta_{y,t}},~~~\lambda=\max\left\{\frac{\kappa}{R_{0}},\frac{\ell\kappa^{2}}{\Delta},\frac{\ell\kappa^{3}}{\epsilon}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where we define</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{y,t}=\max\left\{2,\frac{\lambda^{2}\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}R_{y}^{2}}{5400^{\frac{2}{p}}(\sigma_{f}+\lambda\sigma_{g})^{2}(\ln(B_{y,t}))^{2}}\right\},~~~B_{z,t}=\max\left\{2,\frac{\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}R_{z}^{2}}{5400^{\frac{2}{p}}\sigma_{g}^{2}(\ln(B_{z,t}))^{2}}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>5400</mn><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>5400</mn><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{y,t}=\max\left\{2,\frac{\lambda^{2}\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}R_{y}^{2}}{5400^{\frac{2}{p}}(\sigma_{f}+\lambda\sigma_{g})^{2}(\ln(B_{y,t}))^{2}}\right\},~~~B_{z,t}=\max\left\{2,\frac{\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}R_{z}^{2}}{5400^{\frac{2}{p}}\sigma_{g}^{2}(\ln(B_{z,t}))^{2}}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{y}^{2}\coloneqq 4R_{0}^{2}+\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{32\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}},~~~R_{z}^{2}\coloneqq R_{0}^{2}+\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{2\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{y}^{2}\coloneqq 4R_{0}^{2}+\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{32\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}},~~~R_{z}^{2}\coloneqq R_{0}^{2}+\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{2\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{0}\geq\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|,~~~\Delta=\varphi(x_{0})-\inf_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\varphi(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{0}\geq\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|,~~~\Delta=\varphi(x_{0})-\inf_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\varphi(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then the iterates generated by N<sup id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA satisfy <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla\varphi(\hat{x})\right\|]={\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla\varphi(\hat{x})\right\|]={\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, the overall SFO complexity is bounded by</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta\ell^{\frac{2p-1}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{7p-3}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{4p-2}{p-1}}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta\ell^{\frac{2p-1}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{7p-3}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{4p-2}{p-1}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The main idea of our algorithm is to apply normalized SGD to solve the nonconvex optimization problem <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. In contrast to the settings considered in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu and Zhou [45]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hübler et al. [29]</a></cite>, however, we do not have access to the exact gradient of <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> when dealing with bilevel optimization. Instead, we must account for the error introduced by approximating it through the inner clipped-SGD procedure.
Our general analysis is carried out under the <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-BCM noise condition; in the special case <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=2</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to the standard bounded-variance assumption, Theorem <a href="#S4.EGx7" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.2 Convergence Analysis ‣ 4 Stochastic Bilevel Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> yields an SFO complexity of <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}(\kappa^{11}\sigma^{2}\epsilon^{-6})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>11</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}(\kappa^{11}\sigma^{2}\epsilon^{-6})</annotation></semantics></math>, which aligns with the best-known guarantees of fully first-order methods under the bounded-variance assumption <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">While in-expectation results guarantee small gradient norms when averaged over sufficiently many optimization runs, practical computational constraints often preclude executing a large number of runs.
Hence, a single run that achieves a prescribed gradient norm with high probability are more desirable.
Although the Markov inequality can be used to convert in-expectation guarantees into high-probability guarantees, the resulting dependence on <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is typically polynomially poor, making such bounds impractical.
The following theorem establishes a high-probability guarantee for the N<sup id="S4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA algorithm, with only logarithmic dependence on <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmasm3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Stochastic Gradient Assumption ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, running Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.1 The Algorithm ‣ 4 Stochastic Bilevel Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (N<sup id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA) with</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta_{x}=\sqrt{\frac{\Delta}{\ell\kappa^{3}T}},~~~\eta_{y,t}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{400(L_{f}+\lambda L_{g})\ln\left({16TK}/{\delta}\right)},\frac{2\ln(B_{K})}{\lambda\mu K}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta_{x}=\sqrt{\frac{\Delta}{\ell\kappa^{3}T}},~~~\eta_{y,t}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{400(L_{f}+\lambda L_{g})\ln\left({16TK}/{\delta}\right)},\frac{2\ln(B_{K})}{\lambda\mu K}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta_{z,t}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{400\lambda L_{g}\ln\left({16TK}/{\delta}\right)},\frac{\ln(B_{K})}{\lambda\mu K}\right\},~~~T=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}(\Delta\ell\kappa^{3}\epsilon^{-2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta_{z,t}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{400\lambda L_{g}\ln\left({16TK}/{\delta}\right)},\frac{\ln(B_{K})}{\lambda\mu K}\right\},~~~T=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}(\Delta\ell\kappa^{3}\epsilon^{-2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{3p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right),~~~K=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{4p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right),~~~\lambda=\max\left\{\frac{\kappa}{\sqrt{R}},\frac{\ell\kappa^{2}}{\Delta},\frac{\ell\kappa^{3}}{\epsilon}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><msqrt><mi>R</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{3p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right),~~~K=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{4p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right),~~~\lambda=\max\left\{\frac{\kappa}{\sqrt{R}},\frac{\ell\kappa^{2}}{\Delta},\frac{\ell\kappa^{3}}{\epsilon}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau_{t,k}=\frac{\exp(-\eta_{z,t}\lambda\mu(1+k/2))R_{z}^{2}}{120\eta_{z,t}\ln\left({16TK}/{\delta}\right)},~~~\tau_{t,k}^{\prime}=\frac{\exp(-\eta_{y,t}\lambda\mu(1/2+k/4))R_{y}^{2}}{120\eta_{y,t}\ln\left({16TK}/{\delta}\right)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>120</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>120</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau_{t,k}=\frac{\exp(-\eta_{z,t}\lambda\mu(1+k/2))R_{z}^{2}}{120\eta_{z,t}\ln\left({16TK}/{\delta}\right)},~~~\tau_{t,k}^{\prime}=\frac{\exp(-\eta_{y,t}\lambda\mu(1/2+k/4))R_{y}^{2}}{120\eta_{y,t}\ln\left({16TK}/{\delta}\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where we define</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{y,t}=\max\left\{2,\frac{\lambda^{2}\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}R_{y}^{2}}{5400^{\frac{2}{p}}(\sigma_{f}+\lambda\sigma_{g})^{2}(\ln(B_{y,t}))^{2}\left(\ln\left({16TK}/{\delta}\right)\right)^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>5400</mn><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{y,t}=\max\left\{2,\frac{\lambda^{2}\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}R_{y}^{2}}{5400^{\frac{2}{p}}(\sigma_{f}+\lambda\sigma_{g})^{2}(\ln(B_{y,t}))^{2}\left(\ln\left({16TK}/{\delta}\right)\right)^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{z,t}=\max\left\{2,\frac{\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}R_{z}^{2}}{5400^{\frac{2}{p}}\sigma_{g}^{2}(\ln(B_{z,t}))^{2}\left(\ln\left({16TK}/{\delta}\right)\right)^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>5400</mn><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{z,t}=\max\left\{2,\frac{\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}R_{z}^{2}}{5400^{\frac{2}{p}}\sigma_{g}^{2}(\ln(B_{z,t}))^{2}\left(\ln\left({16TK}/{\delta}\right)\right)^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{y}^{2}\coloneqq 4R_{0}^{2}+\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{32\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}},~~~R_{z}^{2}\coloneqq R_{0}^{2}+\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{2\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{y}^{2}\coloneqq 4R_{0}^{2}+\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{32\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}},~~~R_{z}^{2}\coloneqq R_{0}^{2}+\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{2\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{0}\geq\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|^{2},~~~\Delta=\varphi(x_{0})-\inf_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\varphi(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{0}\geq\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|^{2},~~~\Delta=\varphi(x_{0})-\inf_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\varphi(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then the iterates generated by N<sup id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA satisfy <math id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\nabla\varphi(x_{t})/T={\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\nabla\varphi(x_{t})/T={\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, the total SFO complexity is bounded by</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\dfrac{\Delta\ell^{\frac{2p-1}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{7p-3}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{4p-2}{p-1}}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\dfrac{\Delta\ell^{\frac{2p-1}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{7p-3}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{4p-2}{p-1}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The core idea of our proof is to derive a lower bound on the expected cosine similarity between <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{x,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{x,t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Exploiting the fact that the cosine similarity is bounded within <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, we invoke a high-probability concentration inequality, which yields a mild logarithmic dependence on <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, we remark that the high-probability sample complexity established in Theorem <a href="#S4.EGx10" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.2 Convergence Analysis ‣ 4 Stochastic Bilevel Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> matches that of its in-expectation counterpart in Theorem <a href="#S4.EGx7" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.2 Convergence Analysis ‣ 4 Stochastic Bilevel Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, up to a multiplicative logarithmic factor. Consequently, it also coincides with the best-known SFO complexity of fully first-order stochastic methods under the bounded variance assumption, as established in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. [4]</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Stochastic Minimax Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present a stochastic first-order algorithm for solving the nonconvex-strongly-concave minimax optimization problem and provide the in-expectation and high probability convergence guarantee for solving the problem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Before introducing our algorithm, we note that the stochastic bilevel optimization problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) subsumes the stochastic minimax optimization problem (<a href="#S1.E6" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>). Specifically, when the lower-level function is the negation of the upper-level function, i.e., <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(x,y;\zeta)=-F(x,y;\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(x,y;\zeta)=-F(x,y;\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>, the stochastic bilevel problem reduces to the minimax optimization problem.
Therefore, the results in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Stochastic Bilevel Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> are also applicable to the minimax optimization problem (<a href="#S1.E6" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
However, the SFO complexity of Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.1 The Algorithm ‣ 4 Stochastic Bilevel Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is not tight for minimax optimization.
To address this, we develop a new stochastic algorithm that is specifically tailored for minimax optimization and achieves provable improvements in efficiency.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>The Algorithm</h3>

<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Nested-loop Normalized Stochastic Gradient Descent Ascent (N<sup id="alg2.5" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA)</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}},\hat{y}_{0,0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}},\hat{y}_{0,0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, stepsize <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{x},\eta_{y,t}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{x},\eta_{y,t}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, sequences of clipping parameters <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tau_{t,k}\}_{k=0}^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tau_{t,k}\}_{k=0}^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T,K,M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T,K,M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,\dots,T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,\dots,T-1</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,\dots,K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,\dots,K-1</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
               draw data sample <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{y,t,k}=\nabla_{y}F(x_{t},\hat{y}_{t,k};\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{y,t,k}=\nabla_{y}F(x_{t},\hat{y}_{t,k};\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{t,k+1}=\hat{y}_{t,k}+\eta_{y,t}{\rm clip}(g_{y,t,k},\tau_{t,k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>clip</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{t,k+1}=\hat{y}_{t,k}+\eta_{y,t}{\rm clip}(g_{y,t,k},\tau_{t,k})</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end for</span> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}=\hat{y}_{t,K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}=\hat{y}_{t,K}</annotation></semantics></math>,    <math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{t+1,0}=\hat{y}_{t,K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{t+1,0}=\hat{y}_{t,K}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
              draw a collection of <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> data samples <math id="alg2.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\xi_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\xi_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{g_{x,t}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}}\nabla_{x}F(x_{t},y_{t};\xi_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{g_{x,t}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}}\nabla_{x}F(x_{t},y_{t};\xi_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}=x_{t}-\eta_{x}\cdot\dfrac{g_{x,t}}{\left\|g_{x,t}\right\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}=x_{t}-\eta_{x}\cdot\dfrac{g_{x,t}}{\left\|g_{x,t}\right\|}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end for</span> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
             draw <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg2.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return:</span> <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce our nested-loop normalized stochastic gradient descent–ascent (N<sup id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA) algorithm in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 5.1 The Algorithm ‣ 5 Stochastic Minimax Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Similar to N<sup id="S5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA, the algorithm follows a nested-loop structure: in the outer loop, we perform inexact stochastic gradient descent on the nonconvex function <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, while in the inner loop we approximately solve the maximization problem <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{y}}}f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> for a fixed <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. To mitigate the effect of heavy-tailed noise, we apply clipping to the stochastic gradients evaluated at <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and normalization to the stochastic gradients evaluated at <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A key distinction of our method is that, unlike the N<sup id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA algorithm for bilevel optimization that performs updates on the proxy function <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, N<sup id="S5.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA operates directly on the original function <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This eliminates the reliance on a proxy formulation and yields a stochastic algorithm specifically tailored for minimax optimization with provable efficiency improvements.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Convergence Analysis</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we present the complexity results of N<sup id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA for solving nonconvex–strongly-concave minimax optimization problems.
Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm2" title="Assumption 3.2. ‣ 3.2 Approximate Stationary Points of Minimax Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> and Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmprop2" title="Proposition 3.2 ( [ , Lemma 4.3] ). ‣ 3.2 Approximate Stationary Points of Minimax Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable everywhere and <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ell+\kappa\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ell+\kappa\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth.
To rigorously characterize the convergence behavior of N<sup id="S5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA, we make use of the notion introduced in Definition <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.2 Approximate Stationary Points of Minimax Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.
With these ingredients in place, we formally establish the in-expectation convergence guarantee of our algorithm as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm2" title="Assumption 3.2. ‣ 3.2 Approximate Stationary Points of Minimax Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmasm3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Stochastic Gradient Assumption ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, running Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 5.1 The Algorithm ‣ 5 Stochastic Minimax Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> (N<sup id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA) with</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta_{x}=\frac{\epsilon}{\kappa\ell},~~~\eta_{y,t}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{400\ell},\frac{\ln(B_{t})}{\mu K}\right\},~~~\tau_{t,k}=\frac{\exp(-\eta_{y,t}\mu(1+k/2))R_{y}}{120\eta_{y,t}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>120</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta_{x}=\frac{\epsilon}{\kappa\ell},~~~\eta_{y,t}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{400\ell},\frac{\ln(B_{t})}{\mu K}\right\},~~~\tau_{t,k}=\frac{\exp(-\eta_{y,t}\mu(1+k/2))R_{y}}{120\eta_{y,t}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta_{\Phi}\kappa\ell}{\epsilon^{2}}\right),~~~M=\left(\frac{\sigma}{\epsilon}\right)^{\frac{p}{p-1}},~~~K=\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}\left(\kappa+\left(\frac{\ell^{2}\sigma^{2}}{\mu^{2}\epsilon^{2}}\right)^{\frac{p}{2(p-1)}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta_{\Phi}\kappa\ell}{\epsilon^{2}}\right),~~~M=\left(\frac{\sigma}{\epsilon}\right)^{\frac{p}{p-1}},~~~K=\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}\left(\kappa+\left(\frac{\ell^{2}\sigma^{2}}{\mu^{2}\epsilon^{2}}\right)^{\frac{p}{2(p-1)}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where we define</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{t}=\max\left\{2,\frac{\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}R_{y}^{2}}{5400^{\frac{2}{p}}\sigma^{2}(\ln(B_{t}))^{2}}\right\},~~~\Delta_{\Phi}=\Phi(x_{0})-\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\Phi(x),~~~R_{y}=R_{0}+\frac{4\epsilon}{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>5400</mn><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{t}=\max\left\{2,\frac{\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}R_{y}^{2}}{5400^{\frac{2}{p}}\sigma^{2}(\ln(B_{t}))^{2}}\right\},~~~\Delta_{\Phi}=\Phi(x_{0})-\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\Phi(x),~~~R_{y}=R_{0}+\frac{4\epsilon}{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\geq\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\geq\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the iterates generated by the N<sup id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA algorithm satisfy
<math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla\Phi(\hat{x})\right\|]\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla\Phi(\hat{x})\right\|]\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, the overall SFO complexity is upper bounded by</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\dfrac{\Delta_{\Phi}\kappa^{\frac{2p-1}{p-1}}\ell\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{3p-2}{p-1}}}+\dfrac{\Delta_{\Phi}\kappa^{2}\ell}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\dfrac{\Delta_{\Phi}\kappa^{\frac{2p-1}{p-1}}\ell\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{3p-2}{p-1}}}+\dfrac{\Delta_{\Phi}\kappa^{2}\ell}{\epsilon^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The obtained SFO complexity of N<sup id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA is significantly better than that of N<sup id="S5.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA, which addresses the more general bilevel optimization problem.
Moreover, we can show that the complexity result in Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 5.1. ‣ 5.2 Convergence Analysis ‣ 5 Stochastic Minimax Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> attains the optimal dependence on <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. To further illustrate this point, we consider a special case of the minimax problem in which the objective function takes the form:</p>
<table id="S5.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y)=g(x)+h(y)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y)=g(x)+h(y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is possibly nonconvex and <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly concave, which leads to minimizing on <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and maximizing on <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> are independent.
Consequently, identifying an
<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point of the corresponding function <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> can be reduced to finding an <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point of a nonconvex function <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is constructed based on a stochastic first-order oracle <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla g(x;\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla g(x;\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the analysis of the nonconvex minimization problem under <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-BCM noise condition <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>, <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>, which is based on the stochastic gradient estimator <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla g(x;\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla g(x;\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>, directly implies an <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\epsilon^{-\frac{3p-2}{p-1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\epsilon^{-\frac{3p-2}{p-1}})</annotation></semantics></math> lower bound on our minimax problem.
Formally, we construct a separable objective function of the form <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y)=g(x)+h(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y)=g(x)+h(y)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the nonconvex function constructed in Theorem 6 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. [63]</a></cite>, and <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is an arbitrary smooth, <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly concave function.
It is evident that the lower bound complexity of finding an <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is no smaller than that of finding an <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, which necessitates at least <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\epsilon^{-\frac{3p-2}{p-1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\epsilon^{-\frac{3p-2}{p-1}})</annotation></semantics></math> stochastic gradient evaluations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we provide a high probability convergence guarantee of the N<sup id="S5.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA method for solving the minimax optimization problem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5.2</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm2" title="Assumption 3.2. ‣ 3.2 Approximate Stationary Points of Minimax Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmasm3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Stochastic Gradient Assumption ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, running Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 5.1 The Algorithm ‣ 5 Stochastic Minimax Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> (N<sup id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA) with</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta_{x}=\sqrt{\frac{\Delta_{\Phi}}{(\kappa+1)\ell T}},~~~\eta_{y,t}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{400\ell\ln\left({8TK}/{\delta}\right)},\frac{\ln(B_{t})}{\mu K}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta_{x}=\sqrt{\frac{\Delta_{\Phi}}{(\kappa+1)\ell T}},~~~\eta_{y,t}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{400\ell\ln\left({8TK}/{\delta}\right)},\frac{\ln(B_{t})}{\mu K}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau_{t,k}=\frac{\exp(-\eta_{y,t}\mu(1+k/2))R_{y}}{120\eta_{y,t}\ln\left({8TK}/{\delta}\right)},~~~T=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta_{\Phi}\kappa\ell}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>120</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau_{t,k}=\frac{\exp(-\eta_{y,t}\mu(1+k/2))R_{y}}{120\eta_{y,t}\ln\left({8TK}/{\delta}\right)},~~~T=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta_{\Phi}\kappa\ell}{\epsilon^{2}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M=\left(\frac{\sigma}{\epsilon}\right)^{\frac{p}{p-1}},~~~K=\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}\left(\kappa+\left(\frac{\ell^{2}\sigma^{2}}{\mu^{2}\epsilon^{2}}\right)^{\frac{p}{2(p-1)}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M=\left(\frac{\sigma}{\epsilon}\right)^{\frac{p}{p-1}},~~~K=\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}\left(\kappa+\left(\frac{\ell^{2}\sigma^{2}}{\mu^{2}\epsilon^{2}}\right)^{\frac{p}{2(p-1)}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where we define</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{t}=\max\left\{2,\frac{\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}R_{y}^{2}}{5400^{\frac{2}{p}}\sigma^{2}(\ln(B_{t}))^{2}\left(\ln\left({8TK}/{\delta}\right)\right)^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>5400</mn><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{t}=\max\left\{2,\frac{\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}R_{y}^{2}}{5400^{\frac{2}{p}}\sigma^{2}(\ln(B_{t}))^{2}\left(\ln\left({8TK}/{\delta}\right)\right)^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\Phi}=\Phi(x_{0})-\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\Phi(x),~~~R_{y}=R_{0}+\frac{4\epsilon}{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\Phi}=\Phi(x_{0})-\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\Phi(x),~~~R_{y}=R_{0}+\frac{4\epsilon}{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\geq\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\geq\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the iterates generated by the N<sup id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA method satisfy that
<math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\left\|\nabla\Phi({x}_{t})\right\|_{2}/T\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\left\|\nabla\Phi({x}_{t})\right\|_{2}/T\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, the overall SFO complexity is upper bounded by</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta_{\Phi}\kappa^{\frac{2p-1}{p-1}}\ell\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{3p-2}{p-1}}}+\frac{\Delta_{\Phi}\kappa^{2}\ell}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta_{\Phi}\kappa^{\frac{2p-1}{p-1}}\ell\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{3p-2}{p-1}}}+\frac{\Delta_{\Phi}\kappa^{2}\ell}{\epsilon^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We remark that the high probability sample complexity established in Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5.2 Convergence Analysis ‣ 5 Stochastic Minimax Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> matches the complexity of its in-expectation counterpart up to a multiplicative logarithmic factor.
Consequently, its dependency on <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> also nearly matches the lower bound of the problem.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we conduct numerical experiments to validate the effectiveness of the proposed algorithms on both stochastic minimax and bilevel optimization.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span>A Synthetic Problem</h3>

<figure id="S6.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<table id="S6.F1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S6.F1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.F1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.14952v1/bilinear_game_perfs_pareto_1.2.svg" id="S6.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:177/139;" width="177" height="139"></object></td>
<td id="S6.F1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.14952v1/bilinear_game_perfs_pareto_1.5.svg" id="S6.F1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:177/140;" width="177" height="140"></object></td>
<td id="S6.F1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.14952v1/bilinear_game_perfs_pareto_1.8.svg" id="S6.F1.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:177/140;" width="177" height="140"></object></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.F1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.F1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">(a) <math id="S6.F1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1.2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.F1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">(b) <math id="S6.F1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1.5</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.F1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">(c) <math id="S6.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1.8</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Convergence of several stochastic algorithms (SFO calls) on a synthetic nonconvex–strongly-concave problem with Pareto noise. For <math id="S6.F1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1.5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.8</annotation></semantics></math>, Clipped-SGDMax and N<sup id="S6.F1.4" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA show nearly overlapping performance.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we consider a synthetic nonconvex-strongly-concave minimax optimization problem of the following form:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S6.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\max_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}}m_{1}\left[\left\|x\right\|_{2}^{2}+\sin(3\sqrt{\left\|x\right\|^{2}+1})\right]+x^{\top}Ky-m_{2}\left\|y\right\|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\max_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}}m_{1}\left[\left\|x\right\|_{2}^{2}+\sin(3\sqrt{\left\|x\right\|^{2}+1})\right]+x^{\top}Ky-m_{2}\left\|y\right\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">which can be interpreted as a two-player game <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite> where <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x}=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x}=30</annotation></semantics></math> is the dimension, <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1},m_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1},m_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> are some constants, and the interaction between the two players is modeled through a randomly generated symmetric matrix <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, we set <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=10\tilde{K}/\big\|\tilde{K}\big\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=10\tilde{K}/\big\|\tilde{K}\big\|</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}=(M+M^{\top})/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}=(M+M^{\top})/2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> has entries drawn i.i.d. from a zero-mean Gaussian distribution with variance <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, following the setup of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Laguel et al. [36]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Laguel et al. [37]</a></cite>.
The resulting problem is nonconvex in <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and strongly concave in <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To demonstrate the robustness of our method under heavy-tailed noise, we compare our N<sup id="S6.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA method against several baseline stochastic approaches, including stochastic gradient descent ascent (SGDA) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>, stochastic gradient descent with a max-oracle (SGDmax) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>, <a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite>, and a variant of SGDmax that applies gradient clipping to both the <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>- and <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>-updates.
Although the exact gradient of the problem is available, we deliberately employ a stochastic gradient oracle that generates noisy estimates with perturbations drawn from the heavy-tailed Pareto distribution.
Specifically, for each iteration <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the stochastic gradient as <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla F(x,y,\xi)=\nabla f(x,y)+\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla F(x,y,\xi)=\nabla f(x,y)+\xi</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi=\hat{\xi}-{\mathbb{E}}[\hat{\xi}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi=\hat{\xi}-{\mathbb{E}}[\hat{\xi}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> is i.i.d. drawn from the Pareto distribution with the shape parameter <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
This construction ensures that <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\xi]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\xi]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so the stochastic gradient oracle is unbiased while still exhibiting heavy-tailed noise.
The stepsizes for all algorithms are tuned from the set <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1\times 10^{-6},3\times 10^{-6},1\times 10^{-5}\ldots,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1\times 10^{-6},3\times 10^{-6},1\times 10^{-5}\ldots,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For N<sup id="S6.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA, Clipped-SGDmax, and SGDmax, we fix the number of inner iterations to 10.
We set the total iteration count to <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=5{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=5{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> for N<sup id="S6.SS1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA, Clipped-SGDmax, and SGDmax, and <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=50{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=50{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> for SGDA, so that all methods incur the same total number of stochastic first-order oracle calls.
We perform 20 independent runs for each experiment and present the averaged results.
The convergence performance of these methods under Pareto noise is reported in Figure <a href="#S6.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 6.1 A Synthetic Problem ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. All methods converge rapidly to a neighborhood of the optimal solution. However, while SGDmax and SGDA exhibit pronounced oscillations in their trajectories after some point, N<sup id="S6.SS1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA and Clipped-SGDmax demonstrate markedly more stable convergence behavior in the presence of the heavy-tailed noise.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2 </span>Learnable Regularization</h3>

<figure id="S6.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.14952v1/l2reg_stoc.svg" id="S6.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:519/202;" width="519" height="202"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Comparison of stochastic algorithms on Problem (<a href="#S6.E13" title="In 6.2 Learnable Regularization ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>). </figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we investigate the problem of ”learnable regularization” in logistic regression. The objective is to optimize a feature-wise regularizer, which leads to the following bilevel formulation:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{p}}\left\{\frac{1}{|{\mathcal{D}}^{\rm val}|}\sum_{(a_{i},b_{i})\in{\mathcal{D}}^{\rm val}}\ell(\,\langle a_{i},y^{*}(x)\rangle\,,b_{i})\right\},\\
\text{where }&amp;y^{*}(x)=\arg\min_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{p}}\left\{\frac{1}{|{\mathcal{D}}^{\rm tr}|}\sum_{(a_{i},b_{i})\in{\mathcal{D}}^{\rm tr}}\ell\left(\,\langle a_{i},y\rangle\,,b_{i}\right)+y^{\top}\Sigma(x)\,y\right\},\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>val</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>val</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mtext>where </mtext></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>tr</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>tr</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{p}}\left\{\frac{1}{|{\mathcal{D}}^{\rm val}|}\sum_{(a_{i},b_{i})\in{\mathcal{D}}^{\rm val}}\ell(\,\langle a_{i},y^{*}(x)\rangle\,,b_{i})\right\},\\
\text{where }&amp;y^{*}(x)=\arg\min_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{p}}\left\{\frac{1}{|{\mathcal{D}}^{\rm tr}|}\sum_{(a_{i},b_{i})\in{\mathcal{D}}^{\rm tr}}\ell\left(\,\langle a_{i},y\rangle\,,b_{i}\right)+y^{\top}\Sigma(x)\,y\right\},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\,\cdot\,,\,\cdot\,)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\,\cdot\,,\,\cdot\,)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the cross-entropy loss and <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma(x):={\rm diag}(\exp(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma(x):={\rm diag}(\exp(x))</annotation></semantics></math> specifies the regularizers on each feature.
We evaluate this formulation on the “20 newsgroup” dataset, which has been adopted in prior studies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.
The dataset consists of approximately 18,000 documents spanning 20 different newsgroups. Each document is represented as a <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional vector (<math id="S6.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=101{,}631" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>101,631</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=101{,}631</annotation></semantics></math>), where each coordinate corresponds to the TF-IDF (term frequency–inverse document frequency) of a word.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We compare our N<sup id="S6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA method against HVP-based approaches, including stocBiO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> and VRBO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>]</cite>, as well as gradient-based methods such as F<sup id="S6.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite> and F<sup id="S6.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>BSA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.
For all algorithms, we set the number of inner iterations to 10 and the number of outer iterations to 1,000.
In addition, we tune the Lagrangian parameter <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> over the set <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{10^{1},10^{2},10^{3},10^{4}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{10^{1},10^{2},10^{3},10^{4}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for F<sup id="S6.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SA, F<sup id="S6.SS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>BSA, and N<sup id="S6.SS2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA. The stepsizes of all algorithms are tuned from the set <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{10^{-5},10^{-4},\ldots,10^{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{10^{-5},10^{-4},\ldots,10^{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure a fair and consistent comparison across methods.
The results are presented in Figure <a href="#S6.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 6.2 Learnable Regularization ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, where the dashed line labeled “w/o Reg” corresponds to the performance without tuning any regularizers.
As shown in the figure, our proposed N<sup id="S6.SS2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA method outperforms all existing baselines.
Interestingly, the HVP-based method VRBO exhibits poor performance, which can be attributed to the high computational cost of its HVP oracle evaluations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3 </span>Data Hyper-Cleaning</h3>

<figure id="S6.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<table id="S6.F3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S6.F3.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.F3.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.14952v1/GPT2_0.5.svg" id="S6.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:172/130;" width="172" height="130"></object></td>
<td id="S6.F3.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.14952v1/GPT2_0.9.svg" id="S6.F3.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:172/130;" width="172" height="130"></object></td>
<td id="S6.F3.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.14952v1/GPT2_0.99.svg" id="S6.F3.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:172/130;" width="172" height="130"></object></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.F3.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.F3.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">(a) <math id="S6.F3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.5</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.F3.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">(b) <math id="S6.F3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.9</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.F3.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">(c) <math id="S6.F3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.99</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Comparison of stochastic algorithms on Problem (<a href="#S6.E14" title="In 6.3 Data Hyper-Cleaning ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) under different corruption ratios <math id="S6.F3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we consider a large-scale data hyper-cleaning problem, following the setup of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>. Let <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the parameters of a neural network.
In our experiments, this corresponds to a GPT-2 model with 124M parameters <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite>. The model is trained on a dataset aggregated from multiple sources. The training loss on the <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th data source is denoted by <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\rm tr}^{i}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>tr</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\rm tr}^{i}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of sources. The objective is to learn optimal weights for the different data sources, parameterized by <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that the trained model achieves low validation loss <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\rm val}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\rm val}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This problem can be formulated as a bilevel optimization problem as below.</p>
<table id="S6.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m}}f(x,y)&amp;:=\ell_{\rm val}(y^{*}(x)),\\
\text{where }y^{*}(x)&amp;=\argmin_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{p}}\Big\{\sum_{i=1}^{m}\sigma(x_{i})\ell_{\rm tr}^{i}(y)\Big\}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>tr</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m}}f(x,y)&amp;:=\ell_{\rm val}(y^{*}(x)),\\
\text{where }y^{*}(x)&amp;=\argmin_{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{p}}\Big\{\sum_{i=1}^{m}\sigma(x_{i})\ell_{\rm tr}^{i}(y)\Big\}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Softmax function, <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x_{i})={\exp(x_{i})}/{\sum_{j=1}^{m}\exp(x_{j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x_{i})={\exp(x_{i})}/{\sum_{j=1}^{m}\exp(x_{j})}</annotation></semantics></math> which ensures that the source weights form a probability distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In our experiment, we use the “Alpaca” dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite>, which contains 52,000 instructions paired with demonstration outputs generated by OpenAI’s “text-davinci-003” engine.
Following the setup of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. [4]</a></cite>, we split the dataset into training and validation sets in an 8:2 ratio, and then introduce corruption into the training set at a proportion of <math id="S6.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.
The corruption is implemented by replacing the demonstration outputs with empty strings.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We compare our proposed method N<sup id="S6.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA with F<sup id="S6.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite> and F<sup id="S6.SS3.p4.1.3" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>BSA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.
Stochastic HVP-based methods are not included in the comparison, as adapting them to distributed bilevel optimization is nontrivial <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>. For all algorithms, we use a batch size of 64 and set a fixed penalty parameter <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The results for different corruption ratios <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> are shown in Figure <a href="#S6.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 6.3 Data Hyper-Cleaning ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. As illustrated, our proposed N<sup id="S6.SS3.p4.1.4" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA methods converge significantly faster than F<sup id="S6.SS3.p4.1.5" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SA and F<sup id="S6.SS3.p4.1.6" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>BSA.
These observations align with the empirical findings of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. [63]</a></cite>, which show that the performance of SGD deteriorates in the presence of heavy-tailed noise, whereas gradient clipping and normalization can mitigate this effect and thereby accelerate convergence.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Conclusion and Future Work</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we propose a stochastic algorithm called N<sup id="S7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA for solving nonconvex–strongly-convex bilevel optimization problems in the presence of heavy-tailed noise.
We establish both in-expectation and high-probability convergence guarantees for N<sup id="S7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA under the <math id="S7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-BCM gradient noise assumption. The stochastic first-order (SFO) complexity of our method matches that of the best-known stochastic gradient–based algorithms under the bounded-variance assumption.
Furthermore, we introduce N<sup id="S7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SGDA for addressing nonconvex–strongly-concave minimax optimization problems with heavy-tailed noise, achieving nearly optimal dependence on <math id="S7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Numerical experiments on both synthetic and large-scale real-world datasets confirm the effectiveness and practical advantages of the proposed algorithms.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Studying the lower bound for stochastic first-order algorithms in solving nonconvex–strongly-convex bilevel optimization problems under heavy-tailed noise is an interesting direction for future work.
Another promising avenue is to extend our methodology to handle constrained bilevel and minimax optimization problems.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Supporting Lemmas</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we revisit some technical lemmas that are essential for establishing the convergence guarantee of the proposed algorithms.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hübler et al. [29, Lemma 7]</a></cite>)<span id="A1.Thmlem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{a^{\top}b}{\left\|b\right\|}\geq\left\|a\right\|-2\left\|a-b\right\|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{a^{\top}b}{\left\|b\right\|}\geq\left\|a\right\|-2\left\|a-b\right\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hübler et al. [29, Lemma 10]</a></cite>)<span id="A1.Thmlem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in(1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(1,2]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a martingale difference sequence (MDS), i.e., <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[X_{j}\mid X_{j-1},\dots,X_{1}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[X_{j}\mid X_{j-1},\dots,X_{1}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> a.s. for all <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|X_{j}\right\|^{p}]&lt;\infty\quad{\rm for\,all\quad}j=1,\dots,n." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>all</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|X_{j}\right\|^{p}]&lt;\infty\quad{\rm for\,all\quad}j=1,\dots,n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}\coloneqq\sum_{j=1}^{n}X_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}\coloneqq\sum_{j=1}^{n}X_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|S_{n}\right\|^{p}]\leq 2\sum_{j=1}^{n}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|X_{j}\right\|^{p}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|S_{n}\right\|^{p}]\leq 2\sum_{j=1}^{n}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|X_{j}\right\|^{p}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Durrett [9, Example 4.1.7]</a></cite>)<span id="A1.Thmlem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,{\mathcal{F}},{\mathbb{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega,{\mathcal{F}},{\mathbb{P}})</annotation></semantics></math> be a probability space and <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> be independent random variables mapping to measurable spaces <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E_{1},\Sigma_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E_{1},\Sigma_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E_{2},\Sigma_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E_{2},\Sigma_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.
Furthermore, let <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:E_{1}\times E_{2}\to{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:E_{1}\times E_{2}\to{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a (Lebesgue-)measurable function with <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|h(X,Y)\right\|]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|h(X,Y)\right\|]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[h(X,Y)\mid X]\overset{a.s.}{=}g(X),\quad{\rm where}\quad g(x)\coloneqq{\mathbb{E}}[h(x,Y)]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em">.</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>where</mi><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[h(X,Y)\mid X]\overset{a.s.}{=}g(X),\quad{\rm where}\quad g(x)\coloneqq{\mathbb{E}}[h(x,Y)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma provides an upper bound on the norm of the difference between a minibatch gradient estimator and its expectation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that <math id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f(x,y)={\mathbb{E}}[\nabla F(x,y;\xi)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f(x,y)={\mathbb{E}}[\nabla F(x,y;\xi)]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla F(x,y;\xi)-\nabla f(x,y)\right\|]\leq\sigma^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla F(x,y;\xi)-\nabla f(x,y)\right\|]\leq\sigma^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\nabla F(x,y;\xi_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\nabla F(x,y;\xi_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, then it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|g-\nabla f(x,y)\right\|]\leq\frac{2\sigma}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|g-\nabla f(x,y)\right\|]\leq\frac{2\sigma}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that the minibatch gradient estimator is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\nabla F(x,y;\xi_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\nabla F(x,y;\xi_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We start by controlling the expected deviation of <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> using Lemma <a href="#A1.EGx21" title="Lemma A.2 ( [ , Lemma 10] ). ‣ Appendix A Supporting Lemmas ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.
We define <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j}(x,y)\coloneqq\nabla F(x,y;\xi_{j})-\nabla f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j}(x,y)\coloneqq\nabla F(x,y;\xi_{j})-\nabla f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now note that <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}(x,y),\dots,X_{M}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}(x,y),\dots,X_{M}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> are independent random variables with mean zero and hence a Martingale Difference Sequence (MDS).
Furthermore, note that <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|X_{j}(x,y)\right\|^{p}]\leq\sigma^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|X_{j}(x,y)\right\|^{p}]\leq\sigma^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> by the assumption.
Therefore, we can apply the Lemma <a href="#A1.EGx21" title="Lemma A.2 ( [ , Lemma 10] ). ‣ Appendix A Supporting Lemmas ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> to get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle l(x,y)\coloneqq{\mathbb{E}}\left[\Big\lVert\sum_{j=1}^{M}X_{j}(x,y)\Big\rVert^{p}\right]\leq 2\sum_{j=1}^{M}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|X_{j}(x,y)\right\|^{p}]\leq 2M\sigma^{p}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle l(x,y)\coloneqq{\mathbb{E}}\left[\Big\lVert\sum_{j=1}^{M}X_{j}(x,y)\Big\rVert^{p}\right]\leq 2\sum_{j=1}^{M}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|X_{j}(x,y)\right\|^{p}]\leq 2M\sigma^{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Next we calculate</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|g-\nabla f(x,y)\right\|\mid x,y]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|g-\nabla f(x,y)\right\|\mid x,y]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\Big\lVert\frac{1}{M}\sum_{j=1}^{M}\left(\nabla F(x,y;\xi_{j})-\nabla f(x,y)\right)\Big\rVert\mid x,y\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\Big\lVert\frac{1}{M}\sum_{j=1}^{M}\left(\nabla F(x,y;\xi_{j})-\nabla f(x,y)\right)\Big\rVert\mid x,y\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{M}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\Big\lVert\sum_{j=1}^{M}\left(\nabla F(x,y;\xi_{j})-\nabla f(x,y)\right)\Big\rVert^{p}\mid x,y\right]^{1/p}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{M}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\Big\lVert\sum_{j=1}^{M}\left(\nabla F(x,y;\xi_{j})-\nabla f(x,y)\right)\Big\rVert^{p}\mid x,y\right]^{1/p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">where we applied Jensen’s inequality in the last inequality.
Next we define</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y=(\xi_{1},\dots,\xi_{M})\quad{\rm and}\quad h(x,y,Y)=\Big\lVert\sum_{j=1}^{M}\left(\nabla F(x,y,\xi_{j})-\nabla f(x,y)\right)\Big\rVert^{p}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mi>and</mi><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y=(\xi_{1},\dots,\xi_{M})\quad{\rm and}\quad h(x,y,Y)=\Big\lVert\sum_{j=1}^{M}\left(\nabla F(x,y,\xi_{j})-\nabla f(x,y)\right)\Big\rVert^{p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">and note that <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> are independent.
Hence, we may apply Lemma <a href="#A1.EGx22" title="Lemma A.3 ( [ , Example 4.1.7] ). ‣ Appendix A Supporting Lemmas ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> which yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|g-\nabla f(x,y)\right\|]\leq\frac{1}{M}{\mathbb{E}}[h(x,y,Y)\mid x,y]^{1/p}=\frac{1}{M}l(x,y)^{1/p}\leq\frac{2\sigma}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>l</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|g-\nabla f(x,y)\right\|]\leq\frac{1}{M}{\mathbb{E}}[h(x,y,Y)\mid x,y]^{1/p}=\frac{1}{M}l(x,y)^{1/p}\leq\frac{2\sigma}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In addition, we review some useful properties of convex functions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nesterov et al. [49, Theorem 2.1.5]</a></cite>)<span id="A1.Thmlem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth function, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(x)+\langle\nabla f(x),y-x\rangle+\frac{1}{2\ell}\left\|\nabla f(x)-\nabla f(y)\right\|^{2}\leq f(y)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(x)+\langle\nabla f(x),y-x\rangle+\frac{1}{2\ell}\left\|\nabla f(x)-\nabla f(y)\right\|^{2}\leq f(y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Additionally, suppose that <math id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth convex function, then it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\ell}\left\|\nabla f(x)-\nabla f(y)\right\|^{2}\leq\langle\nabla f(x)-\nabla f(y),x-y\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\ell}\left\|\nabla f(x)-\nabla f(y)\right\|^{2}\leq\langle\nabla f(x)-\nabla f(y),x-y\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any <math id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.6</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nesterov et al. [49, Theorem 2.1.9]</a></cite>)<span id="A1.Thmlem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly convex function, then it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(x)-\nabla f(y),x-y\rangle\geq\mu\left\|x-y\right\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(x)-\nabla f(y),x-y\rangle\geq\mu\left\|x-y\right\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any <math id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The clip operator enjoys the following properties.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.7</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sadiev et al. [56, Lemma 5.1]</a></cite>)<span id="A1.Thmlem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a random vector in <math id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{X}={\rm clip}(X,\tau)\coloneqq\min(1,\tau/\left\|X\right\|)X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{X}={\rm clip}(X,\tau)\coloneqq\min(1,\tau/\left\|X\right\|)X</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\tilde{X}-{\mathbb{E}}[\tilde{X}]\right\|\leq 2\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\tilde{X}-{\mathbb{E}}[\tilde{X}]\right\|\leq 2\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, if for some <math id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in(1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(1,2]</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[X]=x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[X]=x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|X-x\right\|^{p}]\leq\sigma^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|X-x\right\|^{p}]\leq\sigma^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|x\right\|\leq\tau/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|x\right\|\leq\tau/2</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|{\mathbb{E}}[\tilde{X}]-x\right\|\leq\frac{2^{p}\sigma^{p}}{\tau^{p-1}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|{\mathbb{E}}[\tilde{X}]-x\right\|\leq\frac{2^{p}\sigma^{p}}{\tau^{p-1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\tilde{X}-x\right\|^{2}\right]\leq 18\tau^{2-p}\sigma^{p}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\tilde{X}-x\right\|^{2}\right]\leq 18\tau^{2-p}\sigma^{p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\tilde{X}-{\mathbb{E}}[\tilde{X}]\right\|^{2}\right]\leq 18\tau^{2-p}\sigma^{p}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\tilde{X}-{\mathbb{E}}[\tilde{X}]\right\|^{2}\right]\leq 18\tau^{2-p}\sigma^{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we present some technical lemmas for high-probability convergence analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.8</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li and Orabona [38]</a></cite>)<span id="A1.Thmlem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{F}}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{F}}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a filtration and <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Martingale Difference Sequence with respect to <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{F}}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{F}}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Furthermore, for each <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{N}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{N}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable and assume that <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\exp({D_{t}^{2}}/{\sigma_{t}^{2}})\mid{\mathcal{F}}_{t-1}]\leq e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\exp({D_{t}^{2}}/{\sigma_{t}^{2}})\mid{\mathcal{F}}_{t-1}]\leq e</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for all <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{T}D_{t}\leq\frac{3}{4}\lambda\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sigma_{t}^{2}+\frac{1}{\lambda}\ln\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right)\right)\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{T}D_{t}\leq\frac{3}{4}\lambda\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sigma_{t}^{2}+\frac{1}{\lambda}\ln\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right)\right)\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Our proof also uses the following lemma, which is known as the Bernstein inequality for martingale differences <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.9</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the sequence of random variables <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{i}\}_{i\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{i}\}_{i\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math> form a martingale difference sequence, i.e., <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[X_{i}\mid X_{i-1},\dots,X_{1}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[X_{i}\mid X_{i-1},\dots,X_{1}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume that conditional variances <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{i}^{2}\coloneqq{\mathbb{E}}[X_{i}^{2}\mid X_{i-1},\ldots,X_{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}^{2}\coloneqq{\mathbb{E}}[X_{i}^{2}\mid X_{i-1},\ldots,X_{1}]</annotation></semantics></math> exist and are bounded and assume also that there exists a deterministic constant <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|X_{i}|\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|X_{i}|\leq c</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely for all <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for all <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\Big\{|\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}|&gt;b\quad{\rm and}\quad\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}^{2}\leq G\Big\}\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{b^{2}}{2G+2cb/3}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>and</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\Big\{|\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}|&gt;b\quad{\rm and}\quad\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}^{2}\leq G\Big\}\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{b^{2}}{2G+2cb/3}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Stochastic Bilevel Optimization</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we establish the convergence guarantee of the N<sup id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA algorithm for solving the nonconvex–strongly-convex bilevel optimization problem.
We begin by presenting key properties of the bilevel objective function <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and the auxiliary function <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al. [35]</a></cite>)<span id="A2.Thmlem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, for <math id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 2L_{f}/\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 2L_{f}/\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\lambda}(x,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\lambda}(x,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda\mu/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda\mu/2)</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly convex.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. [4]</a></cite>)<span id="A2.Thmlem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, for <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 2L_{f}/\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 2L_{f}/\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\nabla y^{*}(x)\right\|\leq L_{g}/\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\nabla y^{*}(x)\right\|\leq L_{g}/\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\nabla y_{\lambda}^{*}(x)\right\|\leq 4L_{g}/\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\nabla y_{\lambda}^{*}(x)\right\|\leq 4L_{g}/\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. [4]</a></cite>)<span id="A2.Thmlem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, for <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 2L_{f}/\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 2L_{f}/\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, where</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{3}\coloneqq L_{f}+\frac{4L_{f}L_{g}}{\mu}+\frac{C_{f}\rho_{g}}{\mu}+\frac{C_{f}L_{g}\rho_{g}}{\mu^{2}}+L_{g}D_{2}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{3}\coloneqq L_{f}+\frac{4L_{f}L_{g}}{\mu}+\frac{C_{f}\rho_{g}}{\mu}+\frac{C_{f}L_{g}\rho_{g}}{\mu^{2}}+L_{g}D_{2}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>In-Expectation Convergence Guarantee</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To present the in-expectation convergence guarantee of the N<sup id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA algorithm, we first establish the following important lemma about <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmasm3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Stochastic Gradient Assumption ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, for <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 2L_{f}/\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 2L_{f}/\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, the iterates <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{t}\}_{t\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{t}\}_{t\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math> generated by N<sup id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA satisfies the following inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})}{\eta_{x}T}+\frac{4\sigma_{f}+8\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{4\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|y_{t}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})}{\eta_{x}T}+\frac{4\sigma_{f}+8\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{4\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|y_{t}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]}{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{2\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|z_{t}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]}{T}+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{2\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|z_{t}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]}{T}+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Lemma <a href="#A2.EGx33" title="Lemma B.3 ( [ ] ). ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> implies that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t+1})\leq&amp;L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})+\langle\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t}),x_{t+1}-x_{t}\rangle+\frac{D_{3}}{2}\left\|x_{t+1}-x_{t}\right\|^{2}\\
=&amp;L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-\eta_{x}\langle\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t}),\frac{g_{x,t}}{\left\|g_{x,t}\right\|}\rangle+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}}{2}\\
\leq&amp;L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|+2\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-g_{x,t}\right\|+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}}{2},\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t+1})\leq&amp;L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})+\langle\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t}),x_{t+1}-x_{t}\rangle+\frac{D_{3}}{2}\left\|x_{t+1}-x_{t}\right\|^{2}\\
=&amp;L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-\eta_{x}\langle\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t}),\frac{g_{x,t}}{\left\|g_{x,t}\right\|}\rangle+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}}{2}\\
\leq&amp;L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|+2\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-g_{x,t}\right\|+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}}{2},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality is due to Lemma <a href="#A1.EGx19" title="Lemma A.1 ( [ , Lemma 7] ). ‣ Appendix A Supporting Lemmas ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
Telescope the above inequality from <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-1</annotation></semantics></math>, rearrange the terms, and divide both sides by <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{x}T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{x}T</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq\frac{L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})}{\eta_{x}T}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{2\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-g_{x,t}\right\|}{T}+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq\frac{L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})}{\eta_{x}T}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{2\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-g_{x,t}\right\|}{T}+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">By the triangle inequality, one has</span></p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\\
\leq&amp;\Big\|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\nabla F(x_{t},y_{t};\xi_{i})-\nabla f(x_{t},y_{t})\Big\|+\lambda\Big\|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\nabla G(x_{t},y_{t};\zeta_{i})-\nabla g(x_{t},y_{t})\Big\|\\
&amp;+\lambda\Big\|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\nabla G(x_{t},z_{t};\zeta_{i})-\nabla g(x_{t},z_{t})\Big\|+\left\|\nabla f(x_{t},y_{t})-\nabla f(x_{t},y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t}))\right\|\\
&amp;+\lambda\left\|\nabla g(x_{t},y_{t})-\nabla g(x_{t},y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t}))\right\|+\lambda\left\|\nabla g(x_{t},z_{t})-\nabla g(x_{t},y^{*}(x_{t}))\right\|.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="1.600em">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="1.600em">,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="1.600em">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="1.600em">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="1.600em">,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="1.600em">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\\
\leq&amp;\Big\|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\nabla F(x_{t},y_{t};\xi_{i})-\nabla f(x_{t},y_{t})\Big\|+\lambda\Big\|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\nabla G(x_{t},y_{t};\zeta_{i})-\nabla g(x_{t},y_{t})\Big\|\\
&amp;+\lambda\Big\|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\nabla G(x_{t},z_{t};\zeta_{i})-\nabla g(x_{t},z_{t})\Big\|+\left\|\nabla f(x_{t},y_{t})-\nabla f(x_{t},y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t}))\right\|\\
&amp;+\lambda\left\|\nabla g(x_{t},y_{t})-\nabla g(x_{t},y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t}))\right\|+\lambda\left\|\nabla g(x_{t},z_{t})-\nabla g(x_{t},y^{*}(x_{t}))\right\|.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the expectation on both sides of the inequality, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla_{x}L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]\\
\leq&amp;\frac{2\sigma_{f}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+\frac{4\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+(L_{f}+\lambda L_{g}){\mathbb{E}}[\left\|y_{t}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]+\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|z_{t}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]\\
\leq&amp;\frac{2\sigma_{f}+4\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+2\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|y_{t}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]+\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|z_{t}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|],\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla_{x}L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]\\
\leq&amp;\frac{2\sigma_{f}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+\frac{4\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+(L_{f}+\lambda L_{g}){\mathbb{E}}[\left\|y_{t}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]+\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|z_{t}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]\\
\leq&amp;\frac{2\sigma_{f}+4\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+2\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|y_{t}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]+\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|z_{t}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|],\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality follows from Lemma <a href="#A1.EGx23" title="Lemma A.4. ‣ Appendix A Supporting Lemmas ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> and the last inequality is due to the choice of <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 2L_{f}/\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 2L_{f}/\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking expectations on both sides of (<a href="#A2.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 In-Expectation Convergence Guarantee ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>), and subsititing (<a href="#A2.E22" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 In-Expectation Convergence Guarantee ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) into it, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]\leq&amp;\frac{L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})}{\eta_{x}T}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{2{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-g_{x,t}\right\|]}{T}+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}}{2}\\
\leq&amp;\frac{L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})}{\eta_{x}T}+\frac{4\sigma_{f}+8\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{4\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|y_{t}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]}{T}\\
&amp;+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{2\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|z_{t}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]}{T}+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}}{2}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]\leq&amp;\frac{L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})}{\eta_{x}T}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{2{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-g_{x,t}\right\|]}{T}+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}}{2}\\
\leq&amp;\frac{L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})}{\eta_{x}T}+\frac{4\sigma_{f}+8\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{4\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|y_{t}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]}{T}\\
&amp;+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{2\lambda L_{g}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|z_{t}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]}{T}+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}}{2}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we derive an upper bound on the <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-th bounded central moment of the stochastic gradient estimator of <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Stochastic Gradient Assumption ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\nabla_{y}F(x,y;\xi)+\lambda\nabla_{y}G(x,y;\zeta)-\nabla_{y}f(x,y)-\lambda\nabla_{y}g(x,y)\right\|^{p}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\nabla_{y}F(x,y;\xi)+\lambda\nabla_{y}G(x,y;\zeta)-\nabla_{y}f(x,y)-\lambda\nabla_{y}g(x,y)\right\|^{p}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(2\sigma_{f}+2\lambda\sigma_{g})^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(2\sigma_{f}+2\lambda\sigma_{g})^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla F(x,y;\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla F(x,y;\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla G(x,y;\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla G(x,y;\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math> be the stochastic gradient estimators of <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
We can show that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;\left\|\nabla_{y}F(x,y;\xi)+\lambda\nabla_{y}G(x,y;\zeta)-\nabla_{y}f(x,y)-\lambda\nabla_{y}g(x,y)\right\|^{p}\\
\leq&amp;(\left\|\nabla_{y}F(x,y;\xi)-\nabla_{y}f(x,y)\right\|+\lambda\left\|\nabla_{y}G(x,y;\zeta)-\nabla_{y}g(x,y)\right\|)^{p}\\
\leq&amp;2^{p-1}\left\|\nabla F(x,y;\xi)-\nabla f(x,y)\right\|^{p}+2^{p-1}\lambda^{p}\left\|\nabla G(x,y;\zeta)-\nabla g(x,y)\right\|^{p}\\
\leq&amp;2^{p-1}\sigma_{f}^{p}+2^{p-1}\lambda^{p}\sigma_{g}^{p}\\
\leq&amp;2^{p-1}(\sigma_{f}+\lambda\sigma_{g})^{p}\\
\leq&amp;(2\sigma_{f}+2\lambda\sigma_{g})^{p},\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≤</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;\left\|\nabla_{y}F(x,y;\xi)+\lambda\nabla_{y}G(x,y;\zeta)-\nabla_{y}f(x,y)-\lambda\nabla_{y}g(x,y)\right\|^{p}\\
\leq&amp;(\left\|\nabla_{y}F(x,y;\xi)-\nabla_{y}f(x,y)\right\|+\lambda\left\|\nabla_{y}G(x,y;\zeta)-\nabla_{y}g(x,y)\right\|)^{p}\\
\leq&amp;2^{p-1}\left\|\nabla F(x,y;\xi)-\nabla f(x,y)\right\|^{p}+2^{p-1}\lambda^{p}\left\|\nabla G(x,y;\zeta)-\nabla g(x,y)\right\|^{p}\\
\leq&amp;2^{p-1}\sigma_{f}^{p}+2^{p-1}\lambda^{p}\sigma_{g}^{p}\\
\leq&amp;2^{p-1}(\sigma_{f}+\lambda\sigma_{g})^{p}\\
\leq&amp;(2\sigma_{f}+2\lambda\sigma_{g})^{p},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality is due to the triangle inequality, and the second inequality follows from the convexity of <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\cdot\right\|^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\cdot\right\|^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The third inequality is due to Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Stochastic Gradient Assumption ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, and the fourth inequality follows from <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{p}+b^{p}\leq(a+b)^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{p}+b^{p}\leq(a+b)^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> for any positive number <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Then we can establish the in-expectation convergence guarantee of N<sup id="A2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA algorithm.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.EGx7" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.2 Convergence Analysis ‣ 4 Stochastic Bilevel Optimization under Heavy-Tailed Noise ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 3.1 ( [ ] ). ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.EGx33" title="Lemma B.3 ( [ ] ). ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> with the choice of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, and the fact that <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{0}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{0}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)-\nabla\phi(x)\right\|=\epsilon;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\left\|\nabla L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)-\nabla\phi(x)\right\|=\epsilon;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-\inf_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)={\mathcal{O}}(\Delta);" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-\inf_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)={\mathcal{O}}(\Delta);</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\left\|\nabla^{2}L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)\right\|=D_{3}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d_{x}}}\left\|\nabla^{2}L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)\right\|=D_{3}={\mathcal{O}}(\ell\kappa^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">In addition, due to Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 3.1 ( [ ] ). ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we have <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|y_{0}-y^{*}_{\lambda}(x_{0})\right\|^{2}+\left\|y_{0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|^{2}={\mathcal{O}}(R_{0}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|y_{0}-y^{*}_{\lambda}(x_{0})\right\|^{2}+\left\|y_{0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|^{2}={\mathcal{O}}(R_{0}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
It suffices to show that the algorithm can find an <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-first-order stationary point of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is an <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-first-order stationary point of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#A2.EGx34" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.1 In-Expectation Convergence Guarantee ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, we have to bound the terms <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|z_{t}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|z_{t}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|y_{t}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|y_{t}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first consider the term <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|z_{t}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|z_{t}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]</annotation></semantics></math>.
According to Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda g(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda g(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly convex, and we will show that given any <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\geq\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\geq\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{z}_{t,0}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|^{2}]\leq R_{z}^{2}\coloneqq R_{0}^{2}+\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{2\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{z}_{t,0}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|^{2}]\leq R_{z}^{2}\coloneqq R_{0}^{2}+\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{2\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,\dots,T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,\dots,T-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
With these observations, we can invoke Lemma <a href="#A4.EGx105" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ D.1 In-Expectation Convergence Analysis ‣ Appendix D Convergence Analysis of Clipped-SGD ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x,y)=\lambda g(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x,y)=\lambda g(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> to establish the convergence guarantee for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{z}_{t,K}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{z}_{t,K}-y^{*}(x_{t})\right\|^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now prove the equation (<a href="#A2.E25" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ B.1 In-Expectation Convergence Guarantee ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) by induction.
For the base case <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{z}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|^{2}]\leq R_{0}^{2}\leq R_{z}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{z}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|^{2}]\leq R_{0}^{2}\leq R_{z}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by the parameter setting of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> and the initialization that <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}_{0,0}=\hat{y}_{0,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}_{0,0}=\hat{y}_{0,0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let equation (<a href="#A2.E25" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ B.1 In-Expectation Convergence Guarantee ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) holds for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,\ldots,\tilde{t}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,\ldots,\tilde{t}-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the case <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\tilde{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\tilde{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{z}_{\tilde{t},0}-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}})\right\|^{2}\right]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{z}_{\tilde{t},0}-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}})\right\|^{2}\right]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{z}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]+2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}})-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{z}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]+2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}})-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{z}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]+\frac{2L_{g}^{2}}{\mu^{2}}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|x_{\tilde{t}}-x_{\tilde{t}-1}\right\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{z}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]+\frac{2L_{g}^{2}}{\mu^{2}}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|x_{\tilde{t}}-x_{\tilde{t}-1}\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{z}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]+\frac{2L_{g}^{2}\eta_{x}^{2}}{\mu^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{z}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]+\frac{2L_{g}^{2}\eta_{x}^{2}}{\mu^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality follows from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|a+b\right\|^{2}\leq 2\left\|a\right\|^{2}+2\left\|b\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|a+b\right\|^{2}\leq 2\left\|a\right\|^{2}+2\left\|b\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second inequality is due to Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem2" title="Lemma B.2 ( [ ] ). ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.
According to the induction hypothesis (<a href="#A2.E25" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ B.1 In-Expectation Convergence Guarantee ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>), we can apply Lemma <a href="#A4.EGx105" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ D.1 In-Expectation Convergence Analysis ‣ Appendix D Convergence Analysis of Clipped-SGD ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> to show the following convergence result:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{z}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]\leq 2R_{z}^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu K}{30L_{g}}\right)+\frac{2*5400^{\frac{2}{p}}\sigma_{g}^{2}(\ln(B_{z,\tilde{t}-1}))^{2}}{\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msup><mn>5400</mn><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{z}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]\leq 2R_{z}^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu K}{30L_{g}}\right)+\frac{2*5400^{\frac{2}{p}}\sigma_{g}^{2}(\ln(B_{z,\tilde{t}-1}))^{2}}{\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">According to the parameter choice that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\kappa+\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{4p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right)~~~{\rm and}~~~\eta_{x}=\frac{\epsilon}{\ell\kappa^{3}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.990em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>and</mi><mo lspace="0.990em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\kappa+\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{4p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right)~~~{\rm and}~~~\eta_{x}=\frac{\epsilon}{\ell\kappa^{3}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">we can show that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{z}_{\tilde{t},0}-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}})\right\|^{2}\right]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{z}_{\tilde{t},0}-y^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}})\right\|^{2}\right]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{2L_{g}^{2}\eta_{x}^{2}}{\mu^{2}}\leq\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{2\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}}\leq R_{z}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{2L_{g}^{2}\eta_{x}^{2}}{\mu^{2}}\leq\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{2\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}}\leq R_{z}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we complete the induction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, to apply Lemma <a href="#A4.EGx105" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ D.1 In-Expectation Convergence Analysis ‣ Appendix D Convergence Analysis of Clipped-SGD ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> on <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{y}_{t,K}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{y}_{t,K}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>, we can show that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{y}_{t,0}-y^{*}_{\lambda}(x_{t})\right\|^{2}]\leq R_{y}^{2}\coloneqq 4R_{0}^{2}+\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{32\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{y}_{t,0}-y^{*}_{\lambda}(x_{t})\right\|^{2}]\leq R_{y}^{2}\coloneqq 4R_{0}^{2}+\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{32\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,\ldots,T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,\ldots,T-1</annotation></semantics></math> by induction.
For the base case <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}_{\lambda}(x_{0})\right\|^{2}]\leq 2{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|^{2}]+2\left\|y^{*}(x_{0})-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|^{2}\leq 2R_{0}^{2}+2R_{0}^{2}=4R_{0}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}_{\lambda}(x_{0})\right\|^{2}]\leq 2{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|^{2}]+2\left\|y^{*}(x_{0})-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|^{2}\leq 2R_{0}^{2}+2R_{0}^{2}=4R_{0}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality follows from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|a+b\right\|^{2}\leq 2\left\|a\right\|^{2}+2\left\|b\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|a+b\right\|^{2}\leq 2\left\|a\right\|^{2}+2\left\|b\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second inequality is due to Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 3.1 ( [ ] ). ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\geq\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\geq\left\|\hat{y}_{0,0}-y^{*}(x_{0})\right\|</annotation></semantics></math>, and the choice of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let equation (<a href="#A2.E26" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ B.1 In-Expectation Convergence Guarantee ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) holds for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,\dots,\tilde{t}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,\dots,\tilde{t}-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the case <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\tilde{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\tilde{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{y}_{\tilde{t},0}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}})\right\|^{2}\right]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{y}_{\tilde{t},0}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}})\right\|^{2}\right]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{y}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]+2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}})-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{y}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]+2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}})-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{y}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]+\frac{32L_{g}^{2}}{\mu^{2}}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|x_{\tilde{t}}-x_{\tilde{t}-1}\right\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{y}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]+\frac{32L_{g}^{2}}{\mu^{2}}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|x_{\tilde{t}}-x_{\tilde{t}-1}\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{y}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]+\frac{32L_{g}^{2}\eta_{x}^{2}}{\mu^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{y}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]+\frac{32L_{g}^{2}\eta_{x}^{2}}{\mu^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality follows from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|a+b\right\|^{2}\leq 2\left\|a\right\|^{2}+2\left\|b\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|a+b\right\|^{2}\leq 2\left\|a\right\|^{2}+2\left\|b\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second inequality is due to Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem2" title="Lemma B.2 ( [ ] ). ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.
According to the induction hypothesis equation (<a href="#A2.E26" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ B.1 In-Expectation Convergence Guarantee ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>), we can apply Lemma <a href="#A4.EGx105" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ D.1 In-Expectation Convergence Analysis ‣ Appendix D Convergence Analysis of Clipped-SGD ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> and <a href="#A2.EGx35" title="Lemma B.5. ‣ B.1 In-Expectation Convergence Guarantee ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a> to show the following convergence result:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{y}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]\leq 2R_{y}^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu K}{120L_{g}}\right)+\frac{32*5400^{\frac{2}{p}}(\sigma_{f}+\lambda\sigma_{g})^{2}(\ln(B_{y,t}))^{2}}{\lambda^{2}\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>120</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msup><mn>5400</mn><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{y}_{\tilde{t}-1,K}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}-1})\right\|^{2}\right]\leq 2R_{y}^{2}\exp\left(-\frac{\mu K}{120L_{g}}\right)+\frac{32*5400^{\frac{2}{p}}(\sigma_{f}+\lambda\sigma_{g})^{2}(\ln(B_{y,t}))^{2}}{\lambda^{2}\mu^{2}K^{\frac{2(p-1)}{p}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">With the specified choices of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{y}_{\tilde{t},0}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}})\right\|^{2}\right]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|\hat{y}_{\tilde{t},0}-y_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{\tilde{t}})\right\|^{2}\right]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{32L_{g}^{2}\eta_{x}^{2}}{\mu^{2}}\leq\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{32\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}}\leq R_{y}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{32L_{g}^{2}\eta_{x}^{2}}{\mu^{2}}\leq\frac{2\epsilon^{4}}{\ell^{4}\kappa^{6}}+\frac{32\epsilon^{2}}{\ell^{2}\kappa^{4}}\leq R_{y}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">We complete the proof of induction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining equation (<a href="#A2.E23" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 In-Expectation Convergence Guarantee ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>) and the convergence guarantee of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{t,K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{t,K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}_{t,K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}_{t,K}</annotation></semantics></math> by applying Lemma <a href="#A4.EGx105" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ D.1 In-Expectation Convergence Analysis ‣ Appendix D Convergence Analysis of Clipped-SGD ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, we can find an <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-first-order stationary point of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\lambda}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> by choosing the following set of parameters</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta_{x}=\frac{\epsilon}{\ell\kappa^{3}},~~~T={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta\ell\kappa^{3}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right),~~~M={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{3p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right),~~~K=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{4p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta_{x}=\frac{\epsilon}{\ell\kappa^{3}},~~~T={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta\ell\kappa^{3}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right),~~~M={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{3p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right),~~~K=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\ell^{\frac{p}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{4p}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{2p}{p-1}}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=\max\{\sigma_{f},\sigma_{g}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\max\{\sigma_{f},\sigma_{g}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The total SFO complexity is</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle TM+TK=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta\ell^{\frac{2p-1}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{7p-3}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{4p-2}{p-1}}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle TM+TK=\tilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta\ell^{\frac{2p-1}{p-1}}\kappa^{\frac{7p-3}{p-1}}\sigma^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}{\epsilon^{\frac{4p-2}{p-1}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>High-Probability Convergence Guarantee</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we present the proof of the high-probability convergence guarantee of the N<sup id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA method for solving the nonconvex-strongly-convex bilevel optimization problem.
We start by providing a high-probability convergence guarantee of N<sup id="A2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA with a general gradient estimator <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{x,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{x,t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Throughout this section, we denote the natural filtrations of our method by <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}\coloneqq\sigma(g_{x,0},\dots,g_{x,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}\coloneqq\sigma(g_{x,0},\dots,g_{x,t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.6</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmlem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmlem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmlem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x,y,z)=f(x,y)+\lambda\left(g(x,y)-g(x,z)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x,y,z)=f(x,y)+\lambda\left(g(x,y)-g(x,z)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmasm3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Stochastic Gradient Assumption ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, the iterates generated by N<sup id="A2.Thmlem6.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}&amp;\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq\frac{2({\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T}))}{\eta_{x}T}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{4{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})\right\|\right]}{T}+D_{3}\eta_{x}+\\
&amp;\quad\quad\quad\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{4\left\|\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})-\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|}{T}+12\left(\frac{\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|}{T}+\eta_{x}D_{3}\right)\ln\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}&amp;\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq\frac{2({\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T}))}{\eta_{x}T}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{4{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})\right\|\right]}{T}+D_{3}\eta_{x}+\\
&amp;\quad\quad\quad\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{4\left\|\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})-\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|}{T}+12\left(\frac{\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|}{T}+\eta_{x}D_{3}\right)\ln\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{t}\coloneqq\frac{\langle\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t}),g_{x,t}\rangle}{\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\left\|g_{x,t}\right\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{t}\coloneqq\frac{\langle\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t}),g_{x,t}\rangle}{\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\left\|g_{x,t}\right\|}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the cosine angle between <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{x,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{x,t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then according to (<a href="#A2.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 In-Expectation Convergence Guarantee ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), one has</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t+1})\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t+1})\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-\eta_{x}\left\langle\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t}),\frac{g_{x,t}}{\left\|g_{x,t}\right\|}\right\rangle+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-\eta_{x}\left\langle\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t}),\frac{g_{x,t}}{\left\|g_{x,t}\right\|}\right\rangle+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\nu_{t}+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})-\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\nu_{t}+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Telescope the above inequality from <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and rearrange the terms, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\nu_{t}\leq{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}T}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\nu_{t}\leq{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}T}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we use the fact that <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded and hence sharply concentrates around its expectation.
Formally, let <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t}\coloneqq{\mathbb{E}}[\nu_{t}\mid{\mathcal{F}}_{t-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t}\coloneqq{\mathbb{E}}[\nu_{t}\mid{\mathcal{F}}_{t-1}]</annotation></semantics></math> and denote that <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t}\coloneqq-\eta_{x}(\nu_{t}-\psi_{t})\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t}\coloneqq-\eta_{x}(\nu_{t}-\psi_{t})\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale difference sequence with respect to <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\mathcal{F}}_{t}\}_{t\in{\mathbb{N}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\mathcal{F}}_{t}\}_{t\in{\mathbb{N}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Furthermore, noting that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(\frac{D_{t}^{2}}{4\eta_{x}^{2}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|^{2}}\right)=\exp\left(\frac{(\nu_{t}-\psi_{t})^{2}}{4}\right)\leq e," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(\frac{D_{t}^{2}}{4\eta_{x}^{2}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|^{2}}\right)=\exp\left(\frac{(\nu_{t}-\psi_{t})^{2}}{4}\right)\leq e,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">which implies that we may apply Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem8" title="Lemma A.8 ( [ ] ). ‣ Appendix A Supporting Lemmas ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>.
Doing so yields, for all <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\eta_{x}(\psi_{t}-3\chi\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|)\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}T}{2}+\frac{1}{\chi}\ln\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>χ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\eta_{x}(\psi_{t}-3\chi\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|)\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}T}{2}+\frac{1}{\chi}\ln\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">with probability at least <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the smoothness of <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|+D_{3}t\eta_{x}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|+D_{3}t\eta_{x},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">and hence choosing <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi\coloneqq 1/(6(\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|+C_{T}D_{3}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi\coloneqq 1/(6(\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|+C_{T}D_{3}))</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{T}=\eta_{x}^{2}T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{T}=\eta_{x}^{2}T</annotation></semantics></math> yields, with probability at least <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta/2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\eta_{x}\left(\psi_{t}-\frac{1}{2}\right)\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}T}{2}+6(\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|+C_{T}D_{3})\ln\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\eta_{x}\left(\psi_{t}-\frac{1}{2}\right)\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}T}{2}+6(\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|+C_{T}D_{3})\ln\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">By applying Lemma <a href="#A1.EGx19" title="Lemma A.1 ( [ , Lemma 7] ). ‣ Appendix A Supporting Lemmas ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi_{t}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\geq\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|-2{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi_{t}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\geq\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|-2{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})+2\eta_{x}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}T}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})+2\eta_{x}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|]+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}T}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+6(\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|+C_{T}D_{3})\ln\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+6(\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|+C_{T}D_{3})\ln\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex78.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})+2\eta_{x}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})\right\|\right]+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}T}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T})+2\eta_{x}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})\right\|\right]+\frac{D_{3}\eta_{x}^{2}T}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+2\eta_{x}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\left\|\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})-\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|+6(\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|+C_{T}D_{3})\ln\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+2\eta_{x}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\left\|\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})-\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|+6(\eta_{x}\left\|\nabla{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})\right\|+C_{T}D_{3})\ln\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">where we define <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x,y,z)=f(x,y)+\lambda\left(g(x,y)-g(x,z)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x,y,z)=f(x,y)+\lambda\left(g(x,y)-g(x,z)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and we use triangle inequality in the last step.
Dividing both sides by <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{x}T/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{x}T/2</annotation></semantics></math> leads to the desired result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Under an appropriate choice of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can derive the following high-probability lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.7</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmlem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Approximate Stationary Points of Bilevel Optimization ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmasm3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Stochastic Gradient Assumption ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, we choose <math id="A2.Thmlem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{x}=\sqrt{\Delta/D_{3}T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{x}=\sqrt{\Delta/D_{3}T}</annotation></semantics></math> for the N<sup id="A2.Thmlem7.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA algorithm.
Then, with probability at least <math id="A2.Thmlem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta/2</annotation></semantics></math>, the iterates generated by N<sup id="A2.Thmlem7.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>SBA satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex81.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(7+50\ln\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)\right)\frac{\sqrt{\Delta D_{3}}}{\sqrt{T}}+\frac{8\sigma_{f}+16\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{4\left\|\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})-\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|}{T}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(7+50\ln\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)\right)\frac{\sqrt{\Delta D_{3}}}{\sqrt{T}}+\frac{8\sigma_{f}+16\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{4\left\|\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})-\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|}{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th random samples at the <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration.
First note that <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> measurable and <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{1}^{t},\dots,\xi_{M}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{1}^{t},\dots,\xi_{M}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{1}^{t},\dots,\zeta_{M}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{1}^{t},\dots,\zeta_{M}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence we can apply Lemma <a href="#A1.EGx23" title="Lemma A.4. ‣ Appendix A Supporting Lemmas ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> to get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})\right\|\mid{\mathcal{F}}_{t-1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})\right\|\mid{\mathcal{F}}_{t-1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex83.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})\right\|\mid x_{t},y_{t},z_{t}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left\|g_{x,t}-\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})\right\|\mid x_{t},y_{t},z_{t}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex84.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\left\|\nabla_{x}F(x_{t},y_{t};\xi_{i})-\nabla_{x}f(x_{t},y_{t})\right\||x_{t},y_{t},z_{t}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}\left[\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\left\|\nabla_{x}F(x_{t},y_{t};\xi_{i})-\nabla_{x}f(x_{t},y_{t})\right\||x_{t},y_{t},z_{t}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\lambda{\mathbb{E}}\left[\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\left\|\nabla_{x}G(x_{t},y_{t};\zeta_{i})-\nabla_{x}g(x_{t},y_{t})\right\||x_{t},y_{t},z_{t}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\lambda{\mathbb{E}}\left[\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\left\|\nabla_{x}G(x_{t},y_{t};\zeta_{i})-\nabla_{x}g(x_{t},y_{t})\right\||x_{t},y_{t},z_{t}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\lambda{\mathbb{E}}\left[\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\left\|\nabla_{x}G(x_{t},z_{t};\zeta_{i})-\nabla_{x}g(x_{t},z_{t})\right\||x_{t},y_{t},z_{t}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\lambda{\mathbb{E}}\left[\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\left\|\nabla_{x}G(x_{t},z_{t};\zeta_{i})-\nabla_{x}g(x_{t},z_{t})\right\||x_{t},y_{t},z_{t}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex87.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2\sigma_{f}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+\frac{4\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2\sigma_{f}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+\frac{4\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality follows from the triangle inequality, and the second inequality is due to Lemma <a href="#A1.EGx23" title="Lemma A.4. ‣ Appendix A Supporting Lemmas ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> and Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasm3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Stochastic Gradient Assumption ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.
Plugging the above inequality into (<a href="#A2.E27" title="In Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2 High-Probability Convergence Guarantee ‣ Appendix B Stochastic Bilevel Optimization ‣ Stochastic Bilevel Optimization with Heavy-Tailed Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) now yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\left\|\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2({\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T}))}{\eta_{x}T}+\frac{8\sigma_{f}+16\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{4\left\|\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})-\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2({\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{0})-{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{T}))}{\eta_{x}T}+\frac{8\sigma_{f}+16\lambda\sigma_{g}}{M^{\frac{p-1}{p}}}+\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\frac{4\left\|\nabla_{x}\tilde{{\mathcal{L}}}_{\lambda}(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})-\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{\lambda}^{*}(x_{t})\right\|}{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
